-- QuestLocFlavor (generado 2026-10-17): objetivos completos, con dialogos, solo para narrar.
_G.QuestLocFlavor = _G.QuestLocFlavor or {}
QuestLocFlavor[26] = {
[13000]={"Los barguests pueden encontrarse en el oeste de los Campos de Fornost.\
\
Debes derrotar barghests en los Campos de Fornost.","Barghest derrotado (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Completado","Has derrotado a muchos barghests en el oeste de los Campos de Fornost.","Los sabuesos de la sombra","Barghests malvados y corruptos merodean por los Campos de Fornost. Siguen a los muertos y dejan muerte a su paso.","Derrota a barghests en el oeste de los Campos de Fornost (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[13001]={"By your hand, a terrible Nameless entity has been released. By your hand, he must fall.","Inspect the note from Frethi","'${PLAYER}, I charge you with defeating that... fiend! The Shadowed King must not be allowed to live! Since it was by your hand he was released, it is only fitting that it be by your hand that he fall!\
\
'Return to Moria at once, find Frethi, and track down the Shadowed King. We cannot allow him to release Throkhâr his master!'","The Shadowed King has been vanquished!\
\
You should return to King Thorin and inform him of your victory.","The Shadowed King awaits within the Shadowed Cave.\
\
You should complete Askâd-mazal, the Chamber of Shadows, on any difficulty.","You tell King Thorin of your victory over the Shadowed King, and he smiles with pride and relief.\
\
'Thank you for your bravery, hero. You have undoubtedly saved us from a terrible fate. This incident has proven yet again that we must be ever watchful, for there are still terrible evils lurking in the depths, and secrets yet to be uncovered. We at least know the name of one now: Throkhâr. May the day never come that I must send you to defeat THAT monster.'","Complete Askâd-mazal, the Chamber of Shadows","The Shadowed King must be found and defeated, but first, you must find Frethi.\
\
You should return to the Crown Chamber in the Foundations of Stone.","Frethi is missing, but a note addressed to you lies on the floor","Frethi has left you a note in the Crown Chamber.\
\
You should read the note.","'There you are! This is the Shadowed Cave. It has been sealed for as long as anyone can remember, as far back as our records, and farther! I have never seen it like this! It cannot be a coincidence that this would open just as the Shadowed King is let loose! He must be inside! Quickly, let us go after him!'","Frethi left you a note saying he had gone to investigate the Shadowed Cave.\
\
You should find the Shadowed Cave in the Foundations of Stone.","Return to the Crown Chamber","Find Frethi near the Shadowed Cave","Talk to King Thorin","The Shadowed King","There is a note here with your name on it. It reads:\
\
${PLAYER}, I am fine! My injuries were not severe. I went looking for the Shadowed King. I believe he has entered the Shadowed Cave! It is open! Meet me there as soon as you can!\
\
Frethi"},
[13002]={"The other hunter can likely be found further along the road into Tarlang's Crown.\
\
You have discovered the remains of one of the hunters, but it is possible the other survived. You should search for them.","Gordir can be found on the dock on the river Blackroot to the west of Sardol.\
\
You have found the remains of two hunters from Sardol and evidence of a massing corsair force in Tarlang's Crown.","'Both dead....\
\
'I suppose there is no good news left to find, ${PLAYER}. What you speak of in Tarlang's Crown goes beyond my worst fears... it is not simply one man, but instead an army that forms along the Anfalas.\
\
'The time has come to tell Malthellam of these threats.... I only hope something can still be done.'","The missing hunters can be found somewhere along the road through Tarlang's Crown.\
\
Gordir has grown worried about two hunters that ventured into Tarlang's Crown and has asked you to seek them out.","'Where could a wielder of such fell power come from? And what vile plans does he have for the vale?\
\
'As you know, ${PLAYER}, Sardol's hunters have gone missing, but I think you and I both know that spiders alone could not have been cause for so many losses. Two of our hunters went south to Belfalas through Tarlang's Crown, and we have not seen them in days.\
\
'If this invader has come from Tarlang's Crown, I fear for what may have befallen them. Search for them, ${PLAYER}... we could do with some good news for once.'","Patrol the road deeper into Tarlang's Crown","You see tents of strange make and numerous men in the distance","The road through Tarlang's Crown can be found to the south of Sardol in Blackroot Vale.\
\
Having found both hunters slain, you hope to find out what brought about their demise in Tarlang's Crown.","DNT -- will not be seen","Search Tarlang's Crown for the missing hunters","Talk to Gordir","You have discovered a hunter of Sardol, felled as he tried to flee","You were too late to save this hunter who bears grievous bite wounds","The road through Tarlang's Crown has long served as a route to Dol Amroth, but now Gordir of Sardol fears it serves a new, more sinister purpose.","Search Tarlang's Crown for the other missing hunter","The Shattered Crown"},
[13003]={"Grimbold can possibly be found at the Fords of Isen, where the stones make paths across the river.\
\
You should search the Fords of Isen for Grimbold.","Grimbold can likely be found near the Fords of Isen.\
\
You should search around the Fords of Isen for signs of Grimbold.","'Leave me to die, stranger! My prince lies here, and I cannot allow myself to live while the ford lies open to the likes of Saruman.\
\
'Let them kill me here. The great host has already marched, but they are only the beginning. My death is here.'","The Shattered Lord","Search the hill to the south-east of the Fords","Grimbold can likely be found somewhere at the Fords of Isen in the far west of the Westfold.\
\
You should search for Grimold.","Hildith has asked you to look for her husband Grimbold at the Fords of Isen and tell him that he is still loved, despite the harsh words that passed between them.","Search for Grimbold at the river crossing","This side of the cliff is crawling with hostile Uruks","Death is everywhere, and looters defile the bodies of the slain....","Search the hill to the north-east of the Fords","'You have saved Grimbold's home from fire and foes, but I must ask you to do one more favour in his name, since I am unworthy of your help.\
\
'Will you tell him that his wife still loves him? His spirit is surely broken after losing everyone dear to him, and losing his war upon the enemy at the Fords of Isen.\
\
'Please find him and convince him that he still has a life worth living, ${PLAYER}.'","This side of the cliff is crawling with hostile Dunlendings","Find Grimbold at the fords"},
[13004]={"'Ah, sí, saludos. Las piedras aquí me hablan y me cuentan de una antigua lucha que se ha librado aquí en las Tierras Solitarias. Por un lado están los hombres malditos, del mismo tipo que Emelin, condenados por su inacción. Y por el otro lado hay un... \\qPoder\\q, supongo que podrías llamarlo, que reside en Garth Agarwen. Por lo que puedo discernir, estos hombres malditos han intentado corregir lo que resultó de su inacción, pero han fracasado una y otra vez.\
\
'Estos hombres, o más bien estas \\qsombras\\q, no son del todo malvados, como sabes, y mi corazón se conmueve por su situación. Me gustaría ayudarlos a corregir las cosas, para liberarlos de su maldición. ¿Quizás tú podrías ayudar con eso?\
\
'En los últimos días, espíritus malignos han agitado las aguas de los pantanos, tomando la forma de criaturas llamadas aguaoscura. Han aparecido en gran número en Garth Agarwen y han expulsado a muchas de las sombras. Si entraras en Garth Agarwen para derrotar a algunas de las aguaoscura allí y me trajeras sus espadas, las exhibiría y fortalecería la voluntad decaída de estos hombres malditos.'","'¡Increíble! Pensé que vería solo tres o cuatro espadas de aguaoscura, ¡pero has traído las espadas de un ejército! Cuando estos hombres malditos vean que la carne y la sangre pueden derrotar a los monstruos que habitan Garth Agarwen, entonces quizás su voluntad se fortalezca y algún día sean liberados de su maldición.'","El pasado roto","'¡Tu valentía es una inspiración para el espíritu!'","'Te pediría que me trajeras algunas espadas más de aguaoscura. ¡Debemos mostrar a estos hombres malditos que pueden prevalecer en Garth Agarwen!'","'Has hecho bien, ${PLAYER}. ¡Has devuelto la esperanza a estos pobres hombres malditos!'","'¡No hables de destruir a los muertos, pues ¿qué soy yo? Un muerto viviente, sin hogar y débil, despojado de todo lo que hace a un hombre un hombre. ¡Vete!'","'Tu valentía frente a los tumularios de Manosangrienta ha dado coraje a mis hermanos para reanudar la lucha.'","Desde el despertar del mal en Agamaur, los espíritus malignos han agitado las aguas, tomando la forma de aguaoscura.","Recoge espadas de aguaoscura (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El aguaoscura se encuentra por todas partes en Agamaur y Garth Agarwen, muy al norte.\
\
Aric el Intérprete de piedras desea ayudar a los hombres malditos de Arthedain y te ha pedido que destierres el aguaoscura que se encuentra en Agamaur. También te ha pedido que le traigas sus espadas para exhibirlas y fortalecer el espíritu decaído de los hombres malditos.","'¿Has vencido a los aguasoscuras de Agamaur? ¡Quizás la luz de la esperanza no estaba perdida, sino simplemente oculta!'","'Si tu carne mortal puede desafiar las aguas malignas, los espíritus de Arthedain seguramente pueden soportar el terror de la Doncella Roja.'","'Eres una maravilla entre tu especie al contemplar a los muertos que caminan sin temblar.'","'Gracias a ti, ${PLAYER}, por tus esfuerzos, pues liberarán a mis hermanos.'","Espadas de aguaoscura recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva las espadas de aguaoscura a Aric el Intérprete de piedras"},
[13005]={"Scout the northern end of Fushaum Bal","Thurindol can be found on the border of Talath Úrui and Dor Amarth.\
\
You should talk to Thurindol.","'Well met, ${PLAYER}. We have come to the very edge of where those who fall under the banner of Gondor care to tread. I am glad to have your company here on this blasted plain of fire known as Talath Úrui.\
\
'As I recall, when we last spoke, we were fighting side by side at Pelennor. That battle seems a distant memory after what has transpired over the past few days.\
\
'Thurindol told me you arrived to aid us in Mordor. The Rangers think very highly of you. Speak to Thurindol when you have a moment. He will be able to fill you in.'","The Haradrim and Sûhalar here are not quick to attack you","Scout the southern end of Fushaum Bal","Bregdal, a soldier of Gondor, has gone as far into Mordor as any, but is concerned with what lies ahead.","Talk to Thurindol","Complete quests in Fushaum Bal","The Khundolar here seem to abide by some law or code","Dâr Mauzur and Fushaum Bal can be found in Talath Úrui.\
\
You should scout these locations for Thurindol.","'The battle at the Black Gate was hard fought and with little rest, we find ourselves in the belly of Mordor.\
\
'I will not allow my men any farther south into this dreadful land. Fires and soot choke the air. The ground burns through footcloths in mere seconds.\
\
'I ask you to use your skills for us once more and scout the immediate lands so that we know more of what we might encounter.'","You tell Thurindol everything you have seen.\
\
'The encampment of Dâr Mauzur seems mostly vacated? Perhaps it was a staging area for the armies who we fought at the Black Gate.\
\
'Fushaum Bal concerns me. The men there are trying to organize. We will need to maintain vigilance should their efforts progress.\
\
'Still, there are other structures deeper into Mordor that concern me even more.'","Scout Dâr Mauzur","Thurindol can be found on the border of Talath Úrui and Dor Amarth.\
\
You should speak with Thurindol.","The encampment seems largely unoccupied","The Shattered Plateau"},
[13006]={"'I am ready for more training. Shall we begin the hunt?'","Talk to Ides","The Shield-Maiden's Training","'That was not quite what I had in mind, but it is difficult to ignore that it was invaluable first-hand training.\
\
'How fortunate that I had you at my side when things grew perilous, however. Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'","'Striking training-dummies and sparring with squires... these are fine tasks for a novice, but it is not enough. If I am ever to truly progress towards becoming a shield-maiden, I must see real battle.\
\
'I have just such a task in my mind. It is nothing too excessive, mind you, simply a hunt of the local bears. With you at my side, what danger could such beasts pose?'","Ides has planned a training excursion to hunt bears in the nearby woods. She believes that fighting live opponents will give her much-needed experience.","Ides can be found training at the mill, north of the Rohirrim training grounds, at the northern edge of the Norcrofts.\
\
Ides wishes to speak with you following your dangerous training excursion.","Ides can be found training at the mill, north of the Rohirrim training grounds, at the northern edge of the Norcrofts.\
\
Ides would like you to accompany her and to provide assistance in her training venture."},
[13008]={"In a newly blasted cave, you found a pack, shredded and rumpled, on the floor. Could it belong to the missing scout? Its contents may shed some much needed light upon her whereabouts.","Continue searching the pack","Lúmar is waiting to speak with you about what was written on the note you found.\
\
Lúmar is in Ost Arndír.","You found a mostly clean shirt","Read the hastily scrawled note","You should search through the pack for clues.\
\
The pack is on the table next to Lúmar, in Ost Arndír.","Search the pack","Place the pack on the table","The Shredded Pack","While searching through Igerna's pack, you found a hastily scrawled note addressed to Lúmar. You should read the note.\
\
The note is on the table next to Lúmar, in Ost Arndír.","You found a crumpled note!","You should continue searching through the pack for clues.\
\
The pack is on the table next to Lúmar, in Ost Arndír.","You should search the pack","Lúmar,\
\
I was right, there are goblins in Pinnath Gelin! They've been hounding me for hours, but I managed to slip their grasp thus far. I overheard one mentioning a farm with lots of four legged, spotted, dinners walking around. I can only imagine this is referring to Varbris's poor cows. I must go first to Winbury and see what fate has befallen Nordach. I will leave this message with - wait, something draws near\
\
---\
\
The message abruptly cuts off.","Lúmar has asked you to search through the shredded pack that you found for any information that might tie it to Igerna.\
\
You can search through the pack on the table next to Lúmar, in Ost Arndir.","'I fear Igerna has been captured or assaulted, given the state of this bag. What did you find?'","Speak to Lúmar","'The pack you brought looks familiar to the one Igerna uses. Will you search through it to see if you can find anything of import? You can use the table here to do so.'"},
[13009]={"You have brought the leaders of Ambarûl, Khûd Zagin, and Imhûlar together in Iridír. Mizâdi has much to do before Girhâzi and Amalíbi trust her or her leadership.","Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír when you are ready to go","'Now that everyone is here, we must meet to figure out how to fight this Bârshud and oppose his considerable forces.\
\
'I dread this part, ${PLAYER}. I am no good at negotiating, and worse at diplomacy. Yet here we are. We should go inside and join the others.'","Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír","'That went as well as I expected. I wish I chose my words more carefully, but it is something for which I never developed the talent.\
\
'At least we now have a plan for moving against Bârshud. Thank you for your part in aiding us, friend.'","Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír when you are ready to go.","The Sickle, the Lotus, and the Lion","Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír.","'Let us go into the hall and have words with the others. The sooner we do so the sooner we can act to counter this Bârshud.'"},
[13010]={"Perimbant te ha pedido que le traigas un zafiro imbuido que podría permitir que tu arma adquiera una cualidad élfica. El elfo no sabe dónde puedes encontrar un zafiro así.","'La forja escondida entre las ruinas de Barad Morlas, en Eregion, debería ser el lugar idóneo para imbuir a tu arma con la cualidad que buscas.\
\
'Por desgracia, esas ruinas llevan varias semanas en manos de una fuerza de dunlendinos procedentes del sur. Sin embargo, la suerte está de tu lado, pues una compañía de mis hermanos ha partido recientemente para expulsar a los dunlendinos de Barad Morlas y recuperar las tierras que nos pertenecen por derecho.\
\
'Si me traes un zafiro imbuido, que necesitarás para obtener la cualidad que deseas, te enviaré directamente a Barad Morlas. Para cuando llegues, la situación con los dunlendinos debería estar bajo control.'","Lleva el zafiro potenciado a Perimbant","'¡Ah! Has conseguido un zafiro imbuido. Lo incluiré entre los suministros que necesitarás para la batalla en Barad Morlas.\
\
'Cuando tú y tus compañeros tengais todo listo para partir, ven a hablar conmigo. Para entonces ya tendré tus suministros preparados.'","Los elfos de Rivendel han enviado un pequeño contingente de soldados para recuperar las ruinas de Barad Morlas de manos de los dunlendinos del sur. En esas ruinas se encuentra una de las antiguas forjas donde, en tiempos pasados, se forjaron muchos objetos de gran poder.","'Me temo que he recibido malas noticias de los elfos enviados a asaltar Barad Morlas, ${PLAYER}. Aunque el ataque salió tan bien como cabía esperar, y los dunlendinos fueron derrotados sin que se perdiera ni un solo elfo, algunas bajas fueron inevitables.\
\
'Mientras mi pueblo se disponía a atender a los heridos y a fortificar Barad Morlas, una fuerza dunlendina mucho mayor les ha caído encima de forma inesperada. La batalla sigue en pleno apogeo en estos momentos, y no sé cómo va, ¡pero puedo organizar un viaje rápido para acudir en su ayuda si tienes todo listo!\
\
'Si logramos defender Barad Morlas contra este asalto con tu ayuda, seguro que el comandante de allí estará más que encantado de permitirte el uso de nuestras forjas.'","'Me han llegado noticias de que luchaste con gran valentía en el asedio de Barad Morlas y salvaste a muchos elfos. Te doy las gracias de todo corazón, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Ahora déjame ayudarte una vez más. Utilizaré este zafiro potenciado para dotar a tu arma de una cualidad élfica, y veremos qué puedes hacer con ella.'","Lleva un zafiro imbuido a Perimbant","Habla con Perimbant para viajar a Barad Morlas","'Antes de empezar, tendrás que traerme un zafiro imbuido.'","El asedio de Barad Morlas","Perimbant se encuentra en Echad Dúnann, al oeste de las puertas de Moria.\
\
Perimbant te ha pedido que hables con él cuando tengas todo listo para viajar a Barad Morlas, donde una compañía de elfos ha quedado atrapada por un ejército de dunlendinos procedentes del sur.","Encontrarás a Perimbant en Echad Dúnann, al oeste de las puertas de Moria.\
\
Debes volver a ver a Perimbant para completar la mejora de tu arma.","'¡Gracias por derrotar el ataque contra Barad Morlas! ¡Con tu generosidad has salvado la vida a muchos elfos!'","¡Los elfos de Barad Morlas han sido derrotados!","'¿No pudiste imbuir la piedra? Sin un zafiro potenciado, no puedo ayudarte.'"},
[13011]={"The Siege of Emax Dûl","'There's my infiltration partner! I assume Shâra Mizâdi has filled you in on the plan?\
\
'Never has a mission held such importance. Are you ready?'","Mizâdi's allied forces are in place. You must now infiltrate the city with Razâl and open the gates to Emax Dûl.\
\
Talk to Razâl at Mizâdi's hidden camp, Nashûbu, and complete 'Instance: The Siege of Emax Dûl'.","'Our plan is set in motion. Our forces are nearby, and await my order. I have chosen you and Razâl for the most crucial mission of our campaign.\
\
'You are to enter the city through the secret cave system, find the gate-house, and open the gate to the city, allowing our waiting troops to flood in unhindered. We must work quickly, before Góramul Sai can learn of our plans and plug this hole in his defences.\
\
'Kotráka Saiya has shown us the way. Victory now hinges upon you and Razâl opening the gates in time. I know you will not fail.'","Mizâdi's forces now have a foothold of control in Emax Dûl, but Góramul Sai and Bârshud have escaped.\
\
You should talk to Mizâdi outside of Emax Dûl's palace, Ekal-nêbi.","The time has come to bring the fight to the Ordâkhai's own doorstep.","Talk to Mizâdi","'Today's victory is bittersweet. We have a foothold of control in Emax Dûl, but until the prince is defeated, the Ordâkhai will not retreat from Idagâl.'\
\
'We cannot stop to celebrate. We must find Góramul Sai! I swear, I will find Bârshud and deliver the justice he deserves, but it will have to wait for another day.'","Complete 'Instance: The Siege of Emax Dûl'"},
[13012]={"El tercer asalto del ataque final ha comenzado. Intentan pasar por la última puerta.","<rgb=#FF0000>¡Mathi ha muerto!</rgb>","Id a ver a Mathi, comandante de Gondamon.","Rechazad el tercer asalto.","El asedio de Gondamon","Rechazad el segundo asalto.","El último asalto ha comenzado. Son cada vez menos, pero cada vez más feroces. Sobrevivid a esta tormenta, eliminad a su líder, y Gondamon conservará su libertad.","<rgb=#00FF00>El primer asalto ha sido rechazado. Tenéis unos instantes de respiro antes del próximo ataque.</rgb>","Mathi debe sobrevivir al ataque.","'Así que estos son todos los refuerzos que recibo? Supongo que tendremos que apañarnos con lo que hay. Hemos defendido este fuerte tanto tiempo como ha sido posible, pero temo que el próximo asalto sea el último.\
\
'Apostaos en las murallas y dejad que vengan. Quizá aún quede una esperanza de que este día no marque el fin de Gondamon.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Habéis rechazado el segundo asalto. Aprovechad unos instantes de respiro antes del próximo ataque para recuperar el aliento.</rgb>","Rechazad el primer asalto.","Contened el asalto final.","Gondamon es una de las fortalezas más poderosas de los Barbasluengas en las Montañas Azules. Los Duramano y sus aliados trasgos buscan apoderarse de ella.","El segundo asalto del ataque final ha comenzado. El enemigo intenta abrirse paso por la fuerza a través de otra puerta.","Mathi ha liderado la defensa de Gondamon durante todo el asedio. Es vital que os presentéis ante él y descubráis en qué podríais ser de utilidad.","'Gondamon sigue siendo una ciudad libre. Maltrecha, agotada, pero libre. Hemos volcado hasta nuestras últimas fuerzas en la batalla. Temo que, sin tu intervención, la ciudad habría caído. Los Barbasluengas tenemos una gran deuda contigo.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Han intentado abrirse paso por las tres puertas. El próximo asalto será sin duda el último, pero también el más violento.</rgb>","El primer asalto del ataque final ha comenzado. El enemigo no debe derribar los muros."},
[13013]={"Find the central fountain","Find the Erui overlook, south-east of the Hall of the Gentle Hand","Lady Vanyalos has asked you to appreciate the many beautiful sights within Imloth Melui.","Where the Erui comes down from the mountains in great cascades, noise and peacefulness blend into one.","Lady Vanyalos insists that the gardens and arbors of Imloth Melui recall the grandeur of Gondor in its youth, and wants you to remind her of their varied beauties.","Find the tall stone steps in the north","Return to Lady Vanyalos in her hall","The Sights of Gondor's Garden","Lady Vanyalos listens intently as you describe your exploration of her city. When you are finished, she sighs happily.\
\
'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I think I will sleep now, and perhaps I shall dream of the places you have described to me. I am quite transported, in time if not in place, to the years of my youth, when I saw those sights beneath sun-filled skies, with a sun-lit heart.'","'While you tread the paths of Imloth Melui, do not keep your eyes upon your feet! These fair arbors and gardens recall the grandeur of my kingdom's past. I have walked them many times since my youth, and to remember them is the sweetest respite.\
\
'I ask  you to take note of the loveliest sights you see here. When you return to me, you may recount them and so I will relive the pleasures I knew, through your fresh eyes.'","Lady Vanyalos is in her hall on the north-east rise of Imloth Melui, waiting for you to return with descriptions of her city.","Clear water laughs loudly as it spills into the central fountain. Ancient arches peer from behind flower-laden trees.","Here the River Erui courses widely through great arches, crashing in a great fall on its journey south.","It is cool in the shaded path and branches of the pines seem to whisper of things long forgotten.","Find the shaded path that overlooks the River Erui","Blossom, river, and stonework alike are watched over by slope-side ranks of mountain pine.","Find the bridge by the source of the Erui, north-west of Imloth Melui"},
[13014]={"The Silent Mouth","'There is much to discuss with your diplomat, and there is much to do to prepare the camp before our host arrives, but I have a request for you in the mean time, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Some of my men were taken by the Ordâkhai. We believe they are being held in Esh Mêkag, the Silent Mouth. I know little about it, save its reputation: a prison where Men are taken to have their spirits and bodies broken. I sent a scout, Arâniz, to find the prison and to see if he can get our soldiers out, but he has yet to report back. Find him, and see what you can do to help.'","Captain Hanâbu has sent you to find his scout, Arâniz.\
\
You should find him hidden somewhere outside the prison, Esh Mêkag.","Talk to Hidâti","Find Arâniz outside Esh Mêkag","'Who- who goes there? Captain Hanâbu sent you? Oh, thank Ardu! I did not expect to see a friendly face out here.'\
\
You tell Arâniz you were sent to help rescue the Aradûni soldiers from Esh Mêkag.\
\
'Our captured soldiers are inside the prison or the nearby pit-mine somewhere, I am sure of it, but they are not the only ones. The Ordâkhai have sent captured people from all over Shagâna here to work themselves to death. A few of these thralls have managed to escape. I found them first, and they showed me this place. It is not much of a camp, but it is safe.'","'Another woman seeking to overthrow the Ordâkhai, eh? I expect us all to become fast friends!\
\
'Hanâbu hides it well, but I can tell from the way he speaks of her that this Damakhêra Ardu is more than just his superior. I do not think she will be arriving with the host he expects, based on his sullen demeanor. \
\
'I have a feeling we will be meeting her sooner than later to fight this war together. I look forward to hunting the Ordâkhai down with yet another powerful woman with a grudge! Haha!'","'Worry not! I will help the Aradûni cross the desert when they arrive. Now go, for you are needed elsewhere! There are many Beltáni captive in Esh Mêkag, as well. You can tell me of your success when we next meet.'","'Captain Hanâbu seems grateful for our aid. A promising start, but Damakhêra Ardu is not an easy woman to impress. At least, not from what I have heard. From all accounts she is both fearless and ferocious!\
\
'While you are assisting with the situation in Esh Mêkag, I will be negotiating on behalf of our Shâra. Once the Aradûni arrive, we will lead them to our gathering point: Ahâba. Bring anyone you can free from the prison with you when you return. We will need as large a force as we can possibly muster to face the fortress Emax Dûl.'","Talk to Sorkamâl the Forbearing","People from across Shagâna have been captured by the Ordâkhai and sent to work in Esh Mêkag, the Silent Mouth. If freed, these people may be willing to join Mizâdi's cause.","Captain Hanâbu has asked for your getting his soldiers out of Esh Mêkag, the Silent Mouth.\
\
You should talk to your allies before you depart.","Talk to Unusâli"},
[13015]={"Legolas can be found at the ruined encampment in northern Lhingris.\
\
You found the Silent One's victims presented as some kind of offering to the spiders of Lhingris before the Silent One attacked you and fled back into the shadows. You should return to Legolas.","An Orc known as the Silent One has betrayed the inhabitants of Durthang to the children of Shelob, casting the lands of Lhingris and Udûn into turmoil.","Talk to Legolas at the ruined encampment","Follow the trail of Orkish blood in pursuit of the Silent One","Many slain Orcs have been laid at the foot of a massive cluster of spider eggs...","'Nar, not long at all...\
\
'That little sneak... the Silent One... he betrayed us! We were holding against the spiders until he showed up, and some help he was! The Silent One killed my Orcs with his arrows... and took some of them before the spiders got to them...\
\
'Maybe the little rat is bringing them to Shelob... or maybe he's eating them himself!\
\
'I won't beg, but if you find him... kill him! If he finds you... well....\
\
'Now shove off, and let me die in peace!'","The Silent One can likely be found off the road to the south of Durthang with the slain Orcs he took from Durthang.\
\
A dying Uruk has asked you to kill the Silent One, an Orc who has seemingly aligned himself with the spiders of Lhingris.","Dark drops of Orkish blood lead away from Durthang...","The Silent One","'An Orc has slain his own kin to offer tribute to the spiders of Lhingris? These are very strange tidings, my friend. And the Uruk used the name Shelob? It seems Ungwetári is known by that name to the Orcs....\
\
'As for the Silent One, I wonder how he gained such a curious title. Such a name would be well-earned of a skilled archer or huntsman. Ah, but these are Orcs we speak of! Perhaps his tongue was cut from his mouth for some trifle....\
\
'If he truly does mean to serve the spiders of Lhingris, perhaps he can lead us to the lair of this Shelob. There is little time to consider such things here, my friend.'"},
[13020]={"'The Sisters have returned?\
\
'I am still not certain I can believe one so new to our lands, but I wish it true.\
\
'Now then, we must speak of the conflict in the east.'","Disturb the pile of river-stones","'It has been told that there were once Sisters who watched over the lands of Lebennin, each of them inhabiting one of our great rivers. Five Sisters there were, but long has it been since any have shown their faces to our people.\
\
'The Sister of the Gilrain is said to watch over our lands here in Malbarth, and few venture into the forest up-river for we consider them sacred. In your time at Linhir, did you learn of the Sisters?'\
\
You tell Arvaeth of your meeting with Roamingstar and the power she wielded over the river Gilrain.\
\
'I... even I began to doubt, ${PLAYER}. If you speak true, this will be a time of great upheaval and rebirth in Lebennin. Go back to the others! You must tell them of our Sister's return!'","Tell Lendithil the <rgb=#FF0000>story</rgb> of your encounter with Roamingstar","The pile shifts slightly and trembles, but Roamingstar does not appear...","Barchir can be found in Malbarth in western Lebennin.\
\
Although you could not call Roamingstar forth, Arvaeth still believes your tale. You should return to Barchir.","Heartened by your tales of the Sister of the Gilrain, the people of Lebennin hope to draw her forth and beg her aid.","'Do not worry, my friend.\
\
'I still believe you and I would have my folk do the same. I shall tell them of her return to our lands and inspire hope in my kin.\
\
'I think it is time you returned to Barchir, ${PLAYER}... the war in the east only worsens with each passing moment and you are needed there.'","The pile of river-stones can be found on the banks of the Gilrain to the north-west of Malbarth.\
\
Arvaeth has asked you to disturb the pile of river-stones in an attempt to draw Roamingstar forth once more.","Talk to Barchir in Malbarth","Talk to Arvaeth","Talk to Arvaeth by the Gilrain","Arvaeth can be found to the north-west of Malbarth along the banks of the Gilrain in Lebennin.\
\
Roamingstar did not come to the river's edge. You should speak to Arvaeth about what is to be done.","Tell Melawen the <rgb=#FF0000>story</rgb> of your encounter with Roamingstar","Melawen and Lendithil can be found in Malbarth.\
\
Arvaeth has asked you to tell the people of Malbarth of your supposed meeting with the fabled Sister of the Gilrain.","'You are the first we have known of in ages who claims to have seen one of the Sisters, much less spoken to one.\
\
'If you could call her forth before my folk, I do not think the darkest night could break our spirits.\
\
'Disturb the pile of stones we have placed at the river's edge and perhaps she will honour us all by revealing herself!'","The Sisters' Return","Arvaeth can be found to the north-west of Malbarth in Lebennin.\
\
You have told the folk of Malbarth and should now return to Arvaeth near the banks of the Gilrain."},
[13021]={"A mysterious patch of rust coats the ground","Talk to Mervárth","The murder location can be found somewhere in central Lake-town.\
\
You should find the murder location.","'Well, that was certainly illuminating. It appears our Master was murdered by the Lake-town Smugglers!'","The location of the murder can be found somewhere in central Lake-town.\
\
You should investigate the murder location.","Find the murder location","'${PLAYER}? Captain Álarr instructed us to let you investigate the area. You may look, but please do not touch anything. This is where we found the Master last night. We believe the murderer was hiding behind that crate, pushed the Master against the wall, and stabbed him with that knife. Let us know if you find anything worthwhile.'","Talk to one of the guards at the murder location","The location of the murder can be found somewhere in central Lake-town.\
\
You should talk to one of the guards at the murder location.","'With Captain Álarr's blessing, we have access to the murder location! We should make our way there.'","Captain Álarr has allowed you access to the location of the murder. Join Mervárth in investigating the Master's murder!","A red kerchief has been left behind","Is this the murder weapon?","The murder location can be found somewhere in central Lake-town.\
\
You should talk to one of the guards at the location of the murder.","This appears to be the location of the murder","'Rust? No, I don't know anything about the rust. But Mervárth thinks the red kerchief belongs to the Lake-town Smugglers? That is an important piece of information! I will let Captain Álarr know.'","The murder investigation is complete.\
\
You should talk to Mervárth.","The Site of the Murder","Investigate the murder location"},
[13023]={"The Sky Has Fallen","Nâtatharr is in eastern Clovengap.\
\
You should search for Nâtatharr.","'As you move northward, there are many more locations for our map. Please look for Nâtatharr, a giant boulder the size of a hill that was once part of Clovengap's ceiling!\
\
'I will meet you at Bazanmanar, north of here.'","Gerja Defthand is at Bazanmanar, in north-east Clovengap.\
\
You should let Gerja Defthand know that you found Nâtatharr.","When the mountain was sundered, the ceiling of Clovengap crashed to the valley below.","'Welcome back! Did you find Nâtatharr? Was it enormous?'","A very large rock! From the ceiling!","Search for Nâtatharr","Talk to Gerja in Bazanmanar","Much of the wording has faded with time, but it seems to be a poem describing the sundering of Gundabad, and the crumbling of the ceiling of Clovengap and of Nâtatharr, the Ceiling Rock, crashing to the ground below alongside countless other pieces. The latter were used in the construction of the tiers and ramps of Clovengap."},
[13024]={"'Billina está comiendo otra vez, pero todavía parece alterada. Hiciste tan buen trabajo como podía pedirse para que volviera a comer, ¿crees que también podrías tranquilizarla?\
\
'A Pa no le gusta que ande trasteando con Billina, dice que la pongo demasiado nerviosa. Sin embargo, le has caído en gracia. Quizás incluso te contrataría como peón de granja, si te interesara podría venirnos bien la ayuda extra'","Billina eriza las plumas y empieza a emitir agudos sonidos de cacareo. Parece que está preocupada por algo.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>ADVERTENCIA: Esta misión da comienzo a una misión de sesión especial. Se cerrará tu sesión con tu personaje normal y asumirás la apariencia de un PNJ aliado del jugador. No podrás salir de la Comarca con este personaje y obtendrás un conjunto de habilidades únicas para este personaje especial.</rgb>","Billina está en el corral de la Granja de Arenilla.\
\
Deberías comprobar cómo está Billina.","Billina parece un poco menos agitada que antes, pero parece que estuviera esperando algo.","Billina está en el corral de la Granja de Arenilla.\
\
Deberías intentar averiguar qué le pasa a Billina. Es una gallina bastante inteligente.","Billina la gallina parece estar alterada, deberías intentar averiguar qué le pasa.","Examina a Billina","'Billina parece mucho más tranquila ${PLAYER}, ¡gracias!\
\
'Por cierto, ¿viste un gallo extraño en la granja? Creí haber visto uno, pero nunca pude examinarlo bien.'","¡El cielo se nos cae encima!","'No consigo entender qué es lo que tiene tan alterada a Billina'","Wald Arenilla está en el corral de la Granja de Arenilla.\
\
Deberías volver con Wald Arenilla y contarle tu éxito."},
[13025]={"Hay gallineros en la Granja de los Rizopardo, en el camino al este y un poco al norte hacia Aguja, la Granja de los Coto, al este en Delagua, y la Granja del Granjero Maggot, al este y al sur a lo largo del río Brandivino.\
\
Billina te ha pedido que adviertas a los otros gallineros de la Comarca sobre la amenaza de los lobos.","Visita el gallinero de los Coto.","Billina está convencida de que una plaga de lobos ha llegado a la Comarca y está robando gallinas.","'¿Pero qué es eso? ¿Lobos? No, claro que no, aquí en la Comarca. He oído rumores, sí, pero no son más que eso, rumores.\
\
'Las gallinas hablan, ya sabes, y pueden inventar historias disparatadas y fantasiosas. El único Lobo en esta granja es un perro. Y por supuesto, los perros del granjero deben de ser la razón por la que no tenemos lobos. Son buenos protectores.'","Visita el gallinero de los Rizopardo.","Billina está en el patio de la Granja de los Arenilla.\
\
Billina desea hablar contigo.","'¿Lobos aquí, en la Comarca? Los lobos no se han atrevido a llegar tan lejos desde los tiempos antiguos, o eso cuentan las leyendas.\
\
'No sé bien qué podríamos hacer frente a un ataque así. Si hay algo que podamos hacer aquí, háznoslo saber. Dale mis saludos a Billina.'","Visita el gallinero de los Maggot.","'¿Lobos? Claro que he visto a los lobos. ¿Acaso no has mirado a tu alrededor? ¡Casi todo nuestro gallinero ha desaparecido!\
\
'Sin embargo, hubo algunas personas que se llevaron a los supervivientes hasta El Cruce.'","¡El cielo se nos cae encima!","'Oh, hola de nuevo. Estaba empezando a pensar que no regresarías después de traerme ese bonito regalo. Pensé que tal vez te habían llevado uno de esos lobos terribles.\
\
'Hubo un tiempo en que no teníamos que preocuparnos por los lobos. Había tan pocos que el granjero siempre los ahuyentaba cuando intentaban colarse en el gallinero.\
\
'Pero últimamente cada vez más de nosotros han desaparecido. Creo que puede tratarse de travesuras de lobos. ¡Necesitamos un gallo valiente como tú para ir a advertir a los otros gallineros y averiguar exactamente qué está ocurriendo! Hay gallineros en la Granja de los Rizopardo, al este y un poco al norte por el camino a Aguja, la Granja de los Coto, al este en Delagua, y Bamfurlargo, muy al este y al sur, a lo largo del río.'","'¡Debes advertir a los otros gallineros en la Granja de los Rizopardo, la Granja de los Coto y Bamfurlargo!'"},
[13026]={"'The gap in the hills east of here is known as Lang Rhuven. The entire pass is now blockaded and controlled by the Easterlings. Many Easterlings gather there and continue to come through the pass to the east that eventually heads towards Rhûn.\
\
'I hope that you will be able to call upon your allies as they will be needed to thwart the encampment at Lang Rhuven.'","Return to Candúr","Candúr has asked you to gauge the enemy presence in the Slag-hills before dealing with any other nearby threats.","Many foes can be found in and around the Slag-hills.\
\
You should defeat foes within the Slag-hills.","'I fear many strong enemies gather all around us. I must scout the encampment west of here. Would you divert the eyes of the Enemy in the Slag-hills while I learn more about the encampment to the east?\
\
'We shall meet here afterwards and I will share with you what knowledge I have gained.'","Defeat foes in the Slag-hills (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Enemigos derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You should return to Candúr, who can be found at a small Ranger outpost hidden in the Slag-hills.","Las colinas de escoria"},
[13028]={"'The morvul-slaves can be found defending the keep their kind has pillaged -- the Elf-ruins of Dannenglor, to the north of here.'","Talk to Puiguil at the Haunted Inn","The Slave-horde of Dannenglor","Morvul-slaves can be found in Dannenglor, to the north of the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks.\
\
Puiguil has asked you to defeat many morvul-slaves in Dannenglor and collect the tokens of bondage that can be found on them.","'How have you found Mirkwood thus far, randir? It is not to my liking at all. Several of our number have gone missing on a mission to Dannenglor. We know now that the place is rife with merrevail.\
\
'If you find yourself there, you should defeat many of the morvul-slaves and see if you can learn of this morroval-nest. Any interesting relics you come across while in Dannenglor would be of use to me in discerning the nature of these beasts.\
\
'Just be cautious when you go, ${PLAYER}. It bodes ill that our scouts are still missing. I worry very much that this particular mission will be perilous for you.'","'Have you collected any tokens fromt he morvul-slaves?'","Collect tokens of bondage from morvul-slaves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Dangerous morvul-slaves stalk the city of Dannenglor, protecting their kind from intruders.","Puiguil is at the Haunted Inn, in the Dourstocks of Mirkwood, south of Dannenglor.\
\
You should speak with Puiguil and bring him the tokens of the mervyl's allegiance to their family.","'Thank you, randir, for bringing me these. These tokens look to have been crafted by the beasts themselves, for they are very crude. This means that there is a leader among them, binding them to a life of allegiance towards defending their roost.'","Collected tokens of bondage from morvul-slaves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[13029]={"There is still slop to be cleaned up in the kitchens beneath Isengard.","The slop bucket is in the kitchens.\
\
Barkh wants you to squeeze out the rag you used to clean up the slop into the slop bucket in the kitchens.","Your Uruk-hai overseer wants to talk to you.","Return the dirty rag to Barkh","Cleaned up piles of slop (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Piles of slop litter the floor of the kitchens beneath Isengard.\
\
Barkh has given you a rag and the unenviable task of cleaning up after the Uruk-hai.","Barkh is waiting to speak to you in the kitchens beneath Isengard.","Talk to Barkh","You tip the slop into the bucket, and it makes a sickening sound","Talk to your Uruk-hai overseer","'No talking to the prisoners! You are no less a captive than they, and if you weren't in my company, you'd be thrown in a cell to rot. Remember that. One word to Fâsh, and you won't even have the benefit of stretching your legs.\
\
'A different word, and you might call those locked in the cells the lucky ones!'","'Another worm from the surface! I'm of a mind to chop you up for stew... give the boys something they can sink their fangs into!'\
\
Your Uruk-hai overseer grunts sadly, shaking his head with disappointment.\
\
'It's like that, is it?' responds Barkh. 'Too bad. It's not worth my head to cross the Old Man, and once he's done with you, you won't be fit for stew anyway. Take this rag and clean some of the slop off the floors. You might as well be good for something! Once you're done, squeeze that rag out into the slop bucket there.'","'Don't give me that dirty rag! Squeeze it out in the slop bucket! If Sharkû didn't want you, I'd have your head for that!'","Get some slop from the slop bucket in the kitchens","Barkh wants you to get some slop from the slop bucket in the kitchens and bring it to the bucket in the dungeons. The entrance to the dungeons is in the north-west wall of the main cavern.","Barkh manages the kitchens in the south-west wall of the cavern beneath Isengard.\
\
Your overseer wants you to report to the kitchens beneath Isengard for work.","'Why are you just standing there? Get some slop from that bucket and bring it to the slop bucket in the dungeons! The prisoners have to eat, after all!\
\
'The entrance to the dungeons is in the north-west wall of the main cavern. Get moving!'","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","'There's work that needs doing in the kitchens! You think this army feeds itself? There's meat roasting, gruel boiling, and bread baking day and night!'\
\
The Uruk-hai grins, baring his fangs.\
\
'Not that you'll get any of that. Prisoners have their own ration. Barkh'll have something else for you to do, I'd wager. To the kitchens with you! They're in the south-west wall of the cavern, and if you don't make good time, I'll tan your hide!'","'Can you do anything right? The slop bucket is right over there! Squeeze out that rag I gave you into the bucket!'","Clean up piles of slop in the kitchens (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Hey! ${RACE}! Do you know anything about what is going on outside? I am a man of Rohan, Baldgar by name, and I was separated from my men not far from the river. Can you tell me if Rohan is still safe?'\
\
But there are too many guards around, and it is not safe to talk.","Talk to Baldgar in the dungeon","'You could not have done that more slowly if you tried, worm. Still, the slop had to be cleaned, and you cleaned it. There will be more later. There's always more!'\
\
Barkh bares his teeth at you.\
\
'It's time to feed the prisoners. Scoop out some feed from the slop bucket and carry it to the dungeons in the north-west wall of the main cavern. Empty the slop into the bucket by the cells. And be quick about it. The thralls have got to eat! Ha! Ha!'","'Get to it, slime! You clean up that slop with the rag I gave you, or I'll send you back to Fâsh in pieces and let him figure out what to tell the Old Man!\
\
'When you're done, squeeze out that rag into the slop bucket, like before! And you'll do it as many times as I say you'll do it!'","The Slop","One of the prisoners has tried to get your attention. You should talk to him.","Barkh is in the kitchens beneath Isengard, waiting to speak to you.","'You think you're done? You're not done until I say you're done! Clean up more of the slop, then dump it into the slop bucket again!\
\
'You work for Barkh, and Barkh says there's more to be done!'","There is work to be done in the kitchens beneath Isengard.","'Well, get to it! That slop's not going to clean up itself! Use that rag I gave you; you won't be getting another! Once you're done, squeeze out the rag over the slop bucket over there.'","Use the slop bucket in the kitchens to squeeze out the dirty rag","'We will talk later, if we get the opportunity!'"},
[13030]={"Luned is in Galtrev, waiting anxiously to hear of the vicious Wargs that roam the landscape of late.\
\
You should tell Luned that you have brought down many Wargs and their riders and hopefully rooted out the source of the evil that entered these lands.","At the source of the Wargs in Pren Gwydh are goblins training the vicious monsters as steeds, which are then carelessly released into the wild to roam as they wish.","Goronu can be found outside of the Howling Caverns in Pren Gwydh.\
\
You should inform Goronu that you have defeated the chief of the Warg-riders.","The chief of the Warg-riders is somewhere within the Howling Caverns.\
\
You should defeat Mange-rider, the chief of the Warg-riders.","The Slovenly Work of Mange-rider","'Ah, ${PLAYER}! Goronu was just here. He spoke highly of your bravery in driving out the Wargs and their riders at the Howling Caverns. You are a great hero, and the folk of Galtrev will sing of your deeds here!'","'I heard a terrible disturbance within, ${PLAYER}, and feared the worst for you, but you have arrived triumphant! Have you truly defeated the terrifying leader of these creatures?\
\
'I will return to Galtrev at once and tell Luned that we have dealt with the threat of Wargs in Pren Gwydh!'","Talk to Goronu","Talk to Luned in Galtrev","'I believe this goblin-band has a chief somewhere within this camp. They are slovenly, but they are organized as well in their efforts. These Wargs are trained, vicious, and unfortunately intelligent.\
\
'You should defeat whoever or whatever is behind these terrible beasts leaking out into our lands.'","Defeat Mange-rider","'I would help you, ${PLAYER}, but I am only a humble scout, you see. I am sure you will do much better than I.'","Defeated Mange-rider"},
[13031]={"The Slow Hunt","Bráthur can be found at Khadâsh-gâra in Elderslade.\
\
You have set many traps on the outskirts of Khadâsh-gâra. You should return to Bráthur.","'You chose a few spots that I would not have, but... all in all, you have done well.\
\
'It is a relaxing pastime, is it not?'","'I sense that a life so quaint is not your way, traveller.\
\
'For my part, I find there is much joy to be found in simple tasks. Take setting traps, for instance. It is like an even easier... and even slower sort of fishing!\
\
'Here, set these traps about outside Khadâsh-gâra. Perhaps you'll find something unexpected in the work!'","Talk to Bráthur","One of the Want-kin, Bráthur, is an accomplished trapper and enjoys hunting the beasts of Elderslade.","Set traps on the outskirts of Khadâsh-gâra (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Khadâsh-gâra can be found in eastern Elderslade.\
\
Bráthur has asked you to set traps on the outskirts of Khadâsh-gâra."},
[13032]={"Prestadír can be found in the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks, near the abandoned village of Audaghaim.\
\
You should bring the wolf-pelts you have collected to Prestadír, for he wishes to examine them.","Collected wolf-pelts from the Darkrage wolves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The wolves can be found all throughout the Dourstocks. If you do not find them, it is likely that they will come to find you. Keep your wits about you, ${PLAYER}! This is a deadly wood.'","Darkrage wolves wander the Dourstocks, harassing the Malledhrim and their efforts. These bold creatures attack at every opportunity, then swiftly vanish into the black trees beyond the sight of the sharp-eyed Elves.","'Do you hear the howling from the trees, ${PLAYER}? We hear them, but we cannot see them when they wish to be scarce -- nay, not even my long-sighted Elf-friends. The Darkrage wolves of Mirkwood are vicious beasts, and their attacks upon the Malledhrim are ceaseless.\
\
'While they are no match for the Elves of Lórien, I believe they are acting on more than instinct. They harry us day and night and seem more bent on distracting our guards and archers than coming in for an actual kill. Such prey as we are not appealing to these beasts.\
\
'I am not sure what motivates them, but I would see them hindered. You should venture into the Dourstocks and remove the harrying threat of these sly beasts. Please bring me as many hides as you can collect, and I will examine them for anything strange. At the very least, the furs will make hardy provisions for my kindred when I return to them.'","'How many wolves have you killed thus far? They can be found throughout the woods near here.'","'Ah! The skins of the Darkrage wolves! I thank you, friend. I am glad you were able to hunt so many without being hunted yourself. Now, let us see....'\
\
Prestadír takes a hide and examines it long. It seems to be of interest to him, though you cannot perceive that it is anything extraordinary.\
\
'Did you observe the strange pattern of the skin? There are subtle striations all over it, as if branded. I believe these beasts are in the service of the Necromancer.'","Collect wolf-pelts from the Darkrage wolves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Sly Beasts of the Dourstocks","Darkrage wolves can be found throughout the Dourstocks and in Audaghaim.\
\
The Ranger Prestadír has asked you to collect the pelts of several of the evil wolves that harass the Malledhrim-guards.","Bring the wolf-pelts to Prestadír"},
[13033]={"Fredegar Bolger ha estado fabricando y almacenando bombas fétidas alrededor de Nobotella, por si surgiera la necesidad.\
\
Debes recoger todas las bombas fétidas para Fredegar Bolger.","Lanza bombas fétidas a los Fronteros de Lotho (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Cieno de pantano...\
\
'Huevos podridos...\
\
'Glándulas de niquebriques...\
\
'Estiércol fresco...'\
\
Fredegar esboza una sonrisa burlona, encantado con la expresión de tu rostro.\
\
'¿Qué es todo esto? Es sencillo, ${PLAYER}: estos ingredientes que he recogido nos permitirán cambiar las tornas. ¡Voy a preparar una mezcla horrible que hará que Lotho la Pústula salga corriendo de vuelta a los brazos de su madre! Mientras estabas fuera, he preparado algo: ¡una bomba fétida terriblemente potente! ¡A estas alturas, mis amigos habrán seguido mi ejemplo y habrán fabricado una docena más!\
\
'Después de que golpeemos a Lotho y a sus Fronteros con estas bombas fétidas, ¡tendrán que ponerse a remojo en la bañera un año entero antes de que puedan ni pensar en continuar sus planes para cambiar las fronteras de la Comarca! ¡Ahora, reunamos las bombas fétidas y pongamos fin a los planes de Lotho!'","Bombas fétidas recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Ja, esos hobbits huelen fatal! ¡Si eso no le da una lección a Lotho, no sé qué lo hará!\
\
'¡Es hora de enfrentarnos a él, ${PLAYER}, de una vez por todas!'","Los planes de Lotho para cambiar las fronteras de la Comarca Allende deben ser detenidos.","Los Fronteros de Lotho se encuentran en la Comarca Allende.\
\
Debes lanzarles bombas fétidas a los Fronteros de Lotho.","El olor de la revuelta","'¡Bien, lo hicimos, ${PLAYER}! ¡Hemos protegido las fronteras y ahora Lotho va a tener que meterse en una bañera, restregándose en lugar de tramar planes! Ah, eso le hará bien, no hay duda.\
\
'Es un poco preocupante que Lotho haya pensado en emplear a esos sinvergüenzas de Bill Helechal y Harry Madreselva, y con todos estos rufianes por ahí parece que se avecinan días oscuros para la Comarca. Será mejor que nos mantengamos alerta, amigo mío.\
\
'¡Pero gracias de nuevo por unirte a mi pequeña rebelión! Salió mejor de lo que esperaba, pero válgame el cielo, ¡qué contento estoy de que haya terminado ya!'","Recoge bombas fétidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Fredegar Bolger se encuentra en el pueblo de Nobotella.\
\
Debes hablar con Fredegar Bolger.","Habla con Fredegar en Nobotella","El Frontero de Lotho huye, ¡pero la peste persiste!"},
[13039]={"'I will tell you what I fear most. It is not the Orc-host below us, for they look north. No, it is the raiding parties I have seen. Though small in numbers, what they may glean and report back... where we lie undefended and un-pillaged, what farm remains yet unburned... these are troublesome thoughts.\
\
'There are abandoned scouts' camp-fires in the wooded groves along the mountain's feet. If you built smoky fires in these, you might draw small parties of Orcs towards you, and dispatch them before they could go farther south.'","Noises soon appear nearby.\
\
Someone is coming!","Started a smoky fire (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Smoke Lures","There are wooded areas west of the Harlond and the road leading up to it.\
\
Dindal has suggested that you start smoky fires at old camp-fire sites in wooded areas near the Harlond, in order to lure Orc raiding parties to you in small groups.","Dindal the scout can be found high up in a secluded look-out, which can be reached by turning north off the east road from Imloth Melui.\
\
You should return to Dindal and let him know that his plan worked.","Dindal fears the Orc raiding parties that come out from Harlond. Though they are small, they may discover Lossarnach's weak points and report back to the larger force.","'The fires worked as I hoped? This is wonderful news. You have made the Orc host blind and deaf to our lands to the south.'","Start smoky fires (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Dindal"},
[13041]={"Las arañas se encuentran en los Cepos, al sur de Esteldín en la Dehesa del Rey.\
\
Debes derrotar arañas tan rápido como puedas, antes de que el tiempo se acabe.","Araña derrotada (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los Cepos","No has derrotado suficientes arañas a tiempo","Las arañas de los Cepos en la Dehesa del Rey han cubierto este pequeño valle de telarañas pegajosas, creando una trampa potencial para cualquiera lo suficientemente desafortunado para entrar por descuido a este lugar. Sería imprudente permanecer aquí más tiempo del necesario.\
\
Debes derrotar a un buen número de arañas tan rápido como puedas.","Has derrotado rápidamente a un buen número de arañas de la Dehesa del Rey en los Cepos, ayudando a hacer el área cerca de Esteldín más segura y libre de la influencia del mal.","Derrota arañas en los Cepos antes de que se acabe el tiempo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Las arañas de los Cepos en la Dehesa del Rey han cubierto este pequeño valle de telarañas pegajosas, creando una trampa potencial para cualquiera lo suficientemente desafortunado para entrar por descuido a este lugar. Sería imprudente permanecer aquí más tiempo del necesario.","Completado"},
[13043]={"The Snatcher","'Forgive me, ${PLAYER}. After all this time, the memory of that night still pains my heart.'\
\
Atta grasps loosely at his throat and appears to look through you for a moment.\
\
'It is not Old Mad Ubb that the children of Hultvís should fear, but Úbil the Snatcher....'","When Atta was a boy, the creature known as the Snatcher returned to the Vales of Anduin and once again sought to prey on the weak and helpless.","Talk to Atta","Atta can be found in Hultvís.\
\
You have heard the tale of Atta's encounter with Úbil the Snatcher. You should talk to Atta.","'Are you prepared to hear my tale?'","'Many years later, I learned that Beorn had died. \
\
'It was said that the Snatcher was driven off by his kin, but the Snatcher lives longer than Men... longer even than those with the gift of Beorn.\
\
'If ever I dared to leave Hultvís, how can I be certain that Úbil does not still lie in wait for me?'","Atta can be found in Hultvís.\
\
Atta has offered to tell you the tale of the night he encountered Úbil the Snatcher."},
[13044]={"You see nothing unusual. Whatever was here must have gone","Visit the goats south-west of Magla and search for what frightened him","'I should not be out here. I wanted to be a farmer! But my father said I should follow my older brothers, and... well, here I am. And last night... well, I cannot explain it. Something spooked the goats, and I climbed up the ridge to investigate... and that's when I heard it.\
\
'Something was... how can I describe it? It was a sniffling sound, like someone with a cold. But there was something about that snuffling sound that made my blood run cold, and as I approached the milling goats, I saw that I was not the only one disturbed by the sound. The eyes of the goats were wild, and they stamped the ground, desperate to get away from... something.\
\
'Something moved among them, low to the ground. It made no sound but that snuffling, as if it was smelling for something. I ran. I ran and ran, and I feel as if my heart has only now calmed itself. If you decide to visit the goats at the enclosures to the north and to the south-west, use caution! That thing might come back!'","Goats mill about the Wailing Hills in their enclosures to the north and to the south-west of Magla.\
\
Magla had a frightening experience near the goats of the Wailing Hills and wants you to see if there is any sign of what so frightened him.","Visit the goats north of Magla and search for what frightened him","The Sniffling Snuffler","Magla is near the two goat enclosures in the Wailing Hills.\
\
You visited the goats milling about the Wailing Hills but found no sign of the creature that so frightened Magla.","Magla heard something sniffing around the goats in the Wailing Hills, and he cannot explain what about the experience filled him with such terror.","'I suppose I may have imagined it? You didn't see anything there? Just goats?'\
\
You know what Magla saw, but the man is frightened enough without knowing the identity of the creature that sniffed so near to him that night: Nazgûl.\
\
He is slowly becoming more calm, but is still shaken by the experience.\
\
'I am not cut out for this sort of thing, ${PLAYER}. My brothers are bold and courageous, and would certainly not have been as frightened. And my sister! She is a handmaiden at the Golden Hall, in Edoras, and she would have marched right up to that... whatever it was... and given it a tongue-lashing it would not soon forget! Not like me.\
\
'Ah, well. I am the one who is here. I am doing my best. I hope my father and brothers and sister are proud, or will be. Thank you again, friend.'","'Something was sniffing around those goats, and it filled me with terror. If you want to investigate, go to the enclosures to the north and to the south-west. But be careful! That thing might come back!\
\
'Oh, what am I doing here, ${PLAYER}? My hands are better-suited for a hay-fork than for a sword and shield!'"},
[13045]={"Entra en la cueva","You have discovered a cave","A cave full of grim-looking people stands in the High Knolls north of Byre Tor.\
\
You should speak with one of the people.","Head North-east away from Byre Tor, to the tallest peak","Find out what caused the strange weather to appear in Byre Tor","Strange weather has cropped up in Byre Tor.\
\
Something is wrong....","The snows have begun again in Byre Tor...a fierce storm, which likely means one thing. Núrzum is near.","'Ah! I knew someone would find us. It is too late for me, but not for the others....'","You suddenly realize that this sudden burst of frosty air might not be mere coincidence.\
\
You begin to shiver.","A tall craggy peak stands to the north-east.\
\
You should head to the high peak, away from Byre Tor, where your vantage point will be better.","You brace yourself as a rush of cold air passes you.","The Snows Come Again"},
[13047]={"Bruidis has asked you to check on Halnith.\
\
Halnith guards the beacon Nendath, which stands to the east of Tadrent.","The Solitary Beacon-warden","'Would you mind taking these food provisions to Halnith at Nendath? She's been quite vigilant about her guard duties, especially since dissenters have taken to lighting the beacons for their own purposes.\
\
'Still, she must feel lonely. I'm sure she would welcome these provisions, as well as your company.'","Guard duty can be a lonely job.","'Ah, Bruidis sent you? There is no need for her to worry. The silence can be... stifling, at times, but all that matters is keeping troublemakers away from the beacon.\
\
'I have not encountered any issues so far. However...'","Talk to Halnith at Nendath"},
[13049]={"'Los hijos de Elrond deben conocer tus hallazgos aquí, en las Gargantas del Bruinen, pues la amenaza que ambas criaturas representan no puede ser ignorada. ¡Los siervos del Enemigo acampan a nuestras puertas!\
\
'Ay, ni Fimgris ni yo podemos abandonar nuestro puesto aquí. ¿Llevarás noticias de estos males a Elladan y Elrohir? Ellos están acampados en las ruinas de Thorenhad. Solo sigue el camino hacia el este hasta la piedra blanca que sirve de marcador, y luego toma la senda del norte hasta llegar a Thorenhad. Las ruinas se hallan en lo alto del risco que domina la guarida de los osos.'","Habla con Elrohir o Elladan en Thorenhad","'Narlinn hizo bien en enviarte a nosotros. Los males que describes no pueden permitirse en el umbral de Imladris. Elladan y yo nos aseguraremos de que llegue palabra a nuestro padre.\
\
'Por ahora, tenemos algunas tareas en las que puedes ayudarnos...'","'Narlinn hizo bien en enviarte a nosotros. Los males que describes no pueden permitirse en el umbral de Imladris. Elrohir y yo nos aseguraremos de que llegue palabra a nuestro padre.\
\
'Por ahora, tenemos algunas tareas en las que puedes ayudarnos...'","Elladan y Elrohir se encuentran en Thorenhad, al este y al norte del campamento de Narlinn. Puede llegarse a las ruinas siguiendo el camino hacia el este hasta la piedra blanca y tomando el sendero del norte hacia el risco.\
\
Narlinn te ha pedido que lleves noticias de los trolls y del lobo sombrío a Elladan y Elrohir, los hijos de Elrond.","El descubrimiento de los trolls de las cavernas cerca de Thorenhad y del ancestro lobo sombrío ha traído gran preocupación a Narlinn y a Fimgris.","Los Hijos de Elrond"},
[13053]={"Has recogido una muestra pura","Hasta toma la muestra que le has traído y vierte una solución en el frasco, observando la reacción con atención.\
\
'Buen trabajo, ${PLAYER}. ¡Creo que has descubierto la mismísima fuente de todo esto! Ahora dime, ¿dónde la encontraste exactamente?'\
\
Hasta escucha atentamente mientras relatas tus hazañas, asintiendo con la cabeza.\
\
'Creo que necesitaremos hacer algunos preparativos antes de poder profundizar en este asunto. Vuelve a verme más tarde, pues debo consultar con Hethuwen para decidir cómo proceder. Puede que necesite tu ayuda de nuevo en los próximos días. Gracias por tu firme dedicación, ${PLAYER}!'","Hasta te ha pedido encontrar una muestra pura de la sustancia descubierta por Hethuwen, quien investigó a las extrañas criaturas que según rumores se hallan en las Obras Hidráulicas.","Encuentra la fuente de la extraña sustancia","'Ve a Gabil-munz y trae una muestra tan pura como puedas.'","'Hethuwen ha solicitado que se extraiga una muestra pura de la extraña sustancia, directamente de la fuente de nuestras investigaciones. Me temo que debes aventurarte una vez más para cumplir esta tarea, si te es posible.\
\
'La mayor concentración de las criaturas que encontraste se halla alrededor de Gabil-munz. Deberías comenzar tu búsqueda del origen de esta sustancia allí.\
\
'Encuentra un modo de extraer una muestra pura de esa cosa repugnante y tráemela cuando hayas terminado. Hethuwen ha enviado una mezcla junto con algunas instrucciones que servirán para poner a prueba la pureza de lo que traigas. ¡Buena suerte, ${PLAYER}!'","Hasta está en la Bodega Putrefacta, en las Obras Hidráulicas, al noreste de Gabil-munz.\
\
Ahora que has encontrado la fuente de la extraña sustancia y has extraído otra muestra, debes llevársela a Hasta para un estudio más exhaustivo.","Lleva la muestra a Hasta","La Fuente","'Dame algo de tiempo para elaborar un plan, ${PLAYER}. Vuelve más tarde y discutiremos cómo proceder.'","'¿La has encontrado ya, ${PLAYER}? La muestra que buscas debe de estar en algún lugar de Gabil-munz.'","La mayor concentración de criaturas puede encontrarse cerca de Gabil-munz, la gran estructura al suroeste.\
\
Hasta te ha pedido que encuentres el origen de la extraña sustancia y traigas una muestra pura para un análisis más profundo."},
[13054]={"Guto can be found at his encampment in the southern fields of Trum Dreng.\
\
You should tell Guto what you saw when you scouted the encampment.","It would appear that Isengard and the Dragon-clan are working together","This spot has an adequate view","Return to Guto at his encampment","'Have you found any sign of the Dragon-clan's rallying point? According to the map, it is somewhere near here, but perhaps the enemy who drew this map was in error.'","According to the map you captured from the Dragon-clan invaders, a major rallying point lies somewhere nearby.\
\
You should see if you can find the rallying point and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> for any signs of the Dragon-clan.","<rgb=#FF0000>Look</rgb> for the Dragon-clan's rallying point nearby","'I followed the map this far, but I have not yet come upon the Dragon-clan. Perhaps they are further in.\
\
'According to the map, there is a rallying point just here, or perhaps a little to the south. Will you scout around and see if you can find it? It seems that this map is not perfectly accurate.'","Guto studied the map and realized that the Dragon-clan invaders planned to both rally and retreat at one secluded piece of land in Trum Dreng.","'Half-orcs from Isengard, you say? Mixing with the Dragon-clan? And here I thought the Draig-lûth were just looking to skirmish over lands and riches....\
\
'This does not bode well, but perhaps we can stop them. First, we will harry them, then we will strike when they are weak!'","The Source of the Dragons","You were spotted by the Dragon-clan","<rgb=#FF0000>Do not let the enemy see you first</rgb>"},
[13055]={"Find the draug-cave","You should scour the Wódfen for clues to the source of the madness that has overcome the wildlife there.","Draugar can be found in their cave, as well as in the Wódfen at night.\
\
You should purge the Wódfen of the draug-threat.","Defeated draugar in Byrgenstow (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Source of the Madness","Something has caused the creatures of the Wódfen to go mad","Discover the source of the madness in the Wódfen","The madness in the Wódfen appears to have been caused by a strange form of the Dead like none you have seen before","Something has driven the creatures of the Wódfen mad... some to the point of death.","Found the draug-cave","Defeat draugar in Byrgenstow (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The entrance to the draugar's cave must be somewhere in the Wódfen.\
\
You should seek the entrance to the draugar's cave.","Something has driven the creatures of the Wódfen mad... some to the point of death.\
\
You should find the source of the madness."},
[13056]={"Search for rubbish (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","This corpse has been dumped unceremoniously into the water","Oldheart's little bird-friend is dead.\
\
You have found a great deal of filth from the slovenly horde of Orcs and Uruks who have gathered temporarily in this sector of Fangorn.\
\
This poor pond is polluted beyond recognition. The water is not water, but poison. The servants of the White Hand are cruel in even their carelessness.","The tiny bird has died from the fumes of the Orcs' filth","The Source of the Mist","Search for corpses (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You suspect that the little bird sought by Oldheart inhaled the fumes of this foetid pond, and likely died of the poisons.\
\
You should search for the little bird.","This unidentifiable goop has a horrific odour","Search for the bird around the pond","The Orcs and Uruks passing through this area have left filth all around the edges of this poor little pond.\
\
You should investigate what manner of filth pollutes this water.","This pile of Orc-refuse is made up of horrors you don't want to imagine","The source of the mist can likely be found to the west of Oldheart.\
\
You should search for the source to the ugly-looking mist that hangs above the trees.","Found a pond, sweet to look upon, but foul to smell. Orcs have settled here...","You spotted an unwholesome-looking mist not far to the west of the hill, and should investigate its source.","Search for piles of slop (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have found a great deal of filth from the slovenly horde of Orcs and Uruks who have gathered temporarily in this sector of Fangorn.\
\
This poor pond is polluted beyond recognition. The water is not water, but poison. The servants of the White Hand are cruel in even their carelessness.","Find the source of the mist","The Ent gives you a slow and silent stare, his eyes filled to the brim with concern.\
\
You should investigate the source of the unwholesome mist lingering above the treetops, for it creeps awfully close to this fine meadow where Oldheart has set his roots.","Completado"},
[13057]={"Rinsed cloths (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You are correct, I am Iorlas. What brings you to the Gate of the Citadel?'\
\
You explain Ormatar's orders and Iorlas looks increasingly displeased.\
\
'While I appreciate your visit, I can't say I appreciate these orders from Ormatar. This is a disgrace, but I must accept any orders from him. Still, a guard of the Citadel is not usually on cleaning duty. What did I do to deserve this?'\
\
You explain that the Citadel staff is short-handed and Ormatar needs guards to help out.\
\
'I see. Well, perhaps you wouldn't mind coming with me then. The work will go quicker with the two of us. Let us meet at the baths in the Southern Great Guest-house when you are ready.'","Collected dirty drying cloths (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Southern Great Guest-house is near the Citadel.\
\
You should collect dirty cloths from the baths.","Rinse the cloths in a water bucket (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'We finished! I shall complain about my day to my brother the next time I see him. I apologize for taking my frustration out on you. These are difficult times and I feel like I'm often ignored by both my family and superiors.'","The Southern Great Guest-house is near the Citadel.\
\
You should seek out the baths in the Southern Great Guest-house.","The Southern Great Guest-house","Iorlas has been tasked with tidying up the baths at the Southern Great Guest-house. He is upset to receive such a lowly task but is glad to have your company in getting the job done as quick as possible.","Speak with Iorlas","The Southern Great Guest-house is near the Citadel.\
\
You should rinse the cloths in a water bucket.","'If we must do this, then so be it.'","Wash the cloths in a bucket (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Welcome to the baths of the Southern Great Guest-house. It is a rather lovely area when you do not have work to do. I bet you my brother gets all the easy jobs from Ormatar. He is probably sitting at The Splintered Shield, drinking a pint with his Halfling friend. I'm not even supposed to be in the Citadel today. It was only Ormatar's chore that brought me here.\
\
'Well, I suppose we should get to it then.'","Washed cloths (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Iorlas shakes his head at the baths as you enter","Seek out the baths in the Southern Great Guest-house","The Southern Great Guest-house is near the Citadel.\
\
You should clean the cloths in a bucket.","Iorlas can be found at the Southern Great Guest-house near the Citadel.\
\
You should speak to Iorlas.","Collect dirty drying cloths (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[13058]={"You should travel to the Wrackwade and talk to Ningêna.","'Hashtal-gûr, ${PLAYER}. My captain, Ningêna, sent me to seek you out. She would like you to consider helping a man from Khûd Zagin to the south. He is insistent, and I feel she finds him rather irksome. She requests that you come to speak with her at the Wrackwade.'","Talk to Ningêna","Ningêna has sent a Dumûri to find you and relay her request for you to come talk to her at the Wrackwade.","The Southern Visitor","'${PLAYER}, there you are. I see my warrior found you. Your willingness to return is appreciated.'"},
[13059]={"'Few come willingly to Halach these days, traveller.\
\
'The Haradrim seek to oust us from our homes, but they shall not succeed... not while I or the rest of the folk that remain still draw breath.\
\
'If you will help us, we would be honoured to count a ${CLASS} among our number.'","'As I said, I believe this is a matter best left to you and Lord Angbor. The Haradrim pose a dire threat to the people seeking refuge in Tumladen as well as all that dwell within Lossarnach. We must discover what has divided their forces near the Erui!\
\
'Lord Angbor is a man of battle, and I trust he will know what is best. He has since departed Tumladen, but you may find him by the Crossings of Erui if he and his men have not yet crossed into Lossarnach.\
\
'May you be swift, ${PLAYER}.'","Concerned by the unusual tactics of the Haradrim, Lady Terenis hopes you and Lord Angbor can uncover their vile designs before it is too late.","Lord Angbor can likely be found somewhere near the Crossings of Erui in eastern Upper Lebennin.\
\
Lady Terenis has asked you to speak to Lord Angbor about the Haradrim forces near the Erui.","You have arrived at Halach, but it lies in ruin...","'Ah, ${PLAYER}. What has kept you?'\
\
You tell Lord Angbor of the Haradrim's unusual behaviour at the beacon Minlos and Lady Terenis's concerns.\
\
'If their forces became divided at the river, perhaps more of their number have fled into the trees in the south. I know of a settlement to the south called Halach... but my men and I will not travel so far south as we advance to the east. Yet, for once I agree with the Lady, the Haradrim in Upper Lebennin must be defeated if we are to leave these lands behind.\
\
'I ask that you travel to Halach and aid the people there if you are able. It seems we must part ways again, my friend, but let us hope that our paths will align in Lossarnach!'","Travel south to Halach","Search the ruins of Halach for any survivors","Survivors may be found somewhere within Halach in south-eastern Upper Lebennin.\
\
You have arrived at the ruined settlement of Halach, and should now search for survivors.","Halach can be found in south-eastern Upper Lebennin along the Anduin.\
\
Angbor has asked you to secure the southern settlements of Upper Lebennin and uncover the plans of the Haradrim before rejoining him in Lossarnach.","The Southern Way","Talk to Angbor near the Crossings of Erui"},
[13060]={"Search for survivors at The Raided Crofts","Talk to Sigeric","The Spared of Mordor","Gísling hopes that the Orcs have not yet slain his people to the south, but fears that it may already be too late. He wishes for you to try and rescue any crofters that have escaped the Orc invasion.","'${PLAYER}, I know my father has great concern for the safety of his people, but I know not if any could survive an Orc assault with simple farming tools.\
\
'When you reach the southern croft, please search for any survivors. If the Orcs are already upon them, I truthfully hold little hope. Yet, with your aid, perhaps they can be saved....\
\
'Hurry to the south, and rescue any crofters you find!'","'One survived after all? My heart is still heavy with guilt, but at least one life was saved.\
\
'I do not recognize this man, though. Perhaps he has come from the Westfold... no matter, he must join the caravan south.'","Talk to Gísil","The Raided Crofts can be found far to the south-west of Garsfeld.","As you loosen Sigeric's bonds, he begins to run towards Garsfeld","'Untie me! Please!\
\
'They killed everyone - I... I have to get out of here.\
\
'To Garsfeld, you say? Yes... yes, I will go right away... I cannot be here any longer. The families... all of them... gone.'","You have spotted a captured crofter amongst the Orcs that have sacked this croft. It is curious that he has been left alive thus far, but it is probable that will change once the Orcs finish stripping resources from the area.","Gísil can be found inside the mead-hall of Garsfeld.","These crofters also met a grisly end, but in the distance you can see a man slumped against a pole of a house","You have found slain crofters... aid has come too late, but perhaps others can be rescued"},
[13061]={"Khaljûn has requested your aid in investigating disturbing sounds coming from the Blade-horn, an ancient and mysterious structure north of Sormedân. Khaljûn fears something evil has taken hold there.","Investigate the area for more information about the mysterious spirit.","Investigate the area around the disturbed spirit.","Investigate the area around the disturbed spirit","Investigate the area outside the Blade-horn for clues","There seems to be something poking out of the dust","Return to Khaljûn in Sormedân and show him the journal you've found.","It appears to be a journal of some kind, although whose is a mystery","The Spectre and the Shadow","You hear a sharp cry, a voice seemingly in pain!","'You found a journal? This - this is from Mashâr. I don't believe it.'","Return to Khaljûn in Sormedân and show him the journal","Khaljûn, a villager in Sormedân, has requested you investigate the strange sounds coming from near Bâdrasag, the Blade-horn.","'This past fortnight I've gotten precious little sleep. A horrible voice shrieks out at night.\
\
'I believe these sounds come from the Blade-horn. Some know it as Bâdrasag. It is an ancient fortress. There is the stench of evil about the place. I don't want to send anyone there, as I believe the place contains only foul beasts with an ill will. But I long for a full night's sleep.\
\
'Would you investigate the Blade-hold, and determine what cursed creature is making that sound? I would be very much in your debt.'","Pick up the dusty book in the dirt"},
[13065]={"'There is no honour here, no happy moral. But still, we must remember.'","Speak with Khaljûn at Khamósh-engar.","Bow to pay your respects to Mashâr.","Give Khaljûn space for his thoughts at Khamósh-engar","Gather stones for Khaljûn suitable to making a stele in remembrance of his brother.","The Spectre and the Shadow, Part 5","Gathered memorial stones for Khaljûn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gather memorial stones for Khaljûn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I cannot believe he is dead, and to die this way. I - I am at a loss for words.\
\
'Would you help me carve a stone for my brother? It is a tradition of ours... and I could use the company.\
\
'It is the least I can do to remember and honour him. \
\
'Meet me just outside the village, on the hill behind Sormedân. It is a place we call Khamósh-engar.'","Join Khaljûn at Khamósh-engar","Join Khaljûn at Khamósh-engar. Khamósh-engar can be found just outside of Sormedân on the hill.","'Would you gather stones for the memorial? They should be relatively smooth. There should be some nearby. I will fashion them into a memorial for Mashâr.'","Help Khaljûn craft the finished stone to honour Mashâr","'I buried them both.\
\
'But we will only be using the stone for my brother. My father – he does not deserve the honour of being remembered, except as a cautionary tale.\
\
'His hands will be forever stained with my brother's blood, his legacy a curse.'","'Although a bitter brew, I am glad to find out the truth... and to bring peace at last, to Mashâr.\
\
'Thank you. I had not the strength to go on this journey without you.'","Speak with Khaljûn at Khamósh-engar","Give Khaljûn space for his thoughts at Khamósh-engar.","Help Khaljûn craft the finished stone to honour Mashâr.","Bow to pay your respects to Mashâr","Khaljûn has asked for your help in creating a memorial stele for his brother, Mashâr."},
[13066]={"Habla con Clothar Hojarena en el Campamento de Adso","'Muy bien, ven conmigo. Te mostraré dónde vi a ese enorme oso. Pero si lo vemos otra vez, tendrás que protegerme. ¿Estás de acuerdo? ¡Porque, de lo contrario, me quedo aquí mismo, muchas gracias!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no puede completarse con una comunidad.</rgb>","'¿Estás aquí para ayudarnos? ¡Por favor, dime que estás aquí para ayudar!'\
\
Le aseguras a Clothar Hojarena que harás todo lo que esté a tu alcance y le preguntas qué lo aqueja.\
\
'¡Un oso, una cosa enorme y monstruosa! Intentamos no acercarnos demasiado al bosque si podemos evitarlo, pero a veces no hay otra opción y Adso necesita que vayamos bajo el dosel por una razón u otra. Bueno, ayer por la tarde yo estaba justo entre los árboles cuando vi la enorme silueta de un oso avanzando pesadamente hacia mí. ¡Era grande, incluso más grande que tú, y su sola presencia me llenó de terror!'\
\
'Si crees que puedes hacer algo con respecto a este demonio con forma de oso, porque sin duda debe serlo, dímelo y te mostraré dónde vi a la bestia'","'He oído historias sobre cambiaformas, ¡pero nunca pensé que conocería a ${PLAYER:una[f]|uno[m]}! Creo que esperaba que dieran más miedo o que fueran más salvajes, pero pareces una persona bastante agradable. Solo pensé que eras muy ${PLAYER:alta[f]|alto[m]}.\
\
'Mostraste una verdadera compasión por ese oso. No creo que la mayoría de los aventureros hubiera hecho lo mismo: hablar con él en lugar de matarlo, quiero decir. A veces hablar es más difícil, pero diría que el esfuerzo vale la pena si salva la vida de un inocente.\
\
'Bueno, cambiaformas, ¡me abriste los ojos! Creo que ya he tenido suficiente autodescubrimiento por hoy. Ahora me vendría bien una buena porción de tarta de arándanos y una siesta!'","El lenguaje de los animales","Clothar Hojarena dice que la gente del campamento de Adso ha estado aterrorizada por un gran oso que anda merodeando por el Bosque Viejo.","Clothar Hojarena se encuentra en el Campamento de Adso. Lo ayudaste a rastrear al gran oso que lo había aterrorizado y también ayudaste al oso a encontrar consuelo.\
\
Clothar ahora sabe que perteneces a la estirpe de Beorn y le está costando adaptarse a ese conocimiento.","Clothar Hojarena se encuentra en el Campamento de Adso y quiere que investigues al gran oso que lo aterrorizó.","Habla con Clothar Hojarena y te mostrará dónde vio al gran oso"},
[13068]={"Defeat spiders in Torech Ungol (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The spider-horde has completely overrun Torech Ungol.\
\
You should defeat spiders in Torech Ungol.","'From Frodo and Sam's accounts, Torech Ungol should be empty. They found no living beings inside save Ungwetári herself. That is no longer the case, as she has recalled all of her children from the wider world. I do not know if she has done this for sustenance, protection, or loneliness. I cannot pretend to fathom the mind of such an ancient and evil being as she. It matters not, the spiders are a threat and must be thinned before we enter deeper into the tunnels.'","'You have done well, ${PLAYER}. Atli will be happy to hear there are fewer spiders in the world. Alas, there will be many more to slay in our near future. The horde is nigh unending.'","The Spider-horde of Torech Ungol","Legolas is standing by outside Torech Ungol.\
\
You should talk to Legolas.","Habla con Legolas.","Defeated spiders in Torech Ungol (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Shelob's lair has become infested with her spider children. Legolas has asked you to thin their numbers."},
[13069]={"A Fastarr se le puede encontrar en el Campamento del Mirador de la Gran Excavación, en Moria.\
\
Fastarr te ha pedido que viajes a la armería de sus antepasados y rescates a sus parientes, atrapados en su interior por las voraces arañas que los han capturado.","A Fastarr se le puede encontrar en el Campamento del Mirador de la Gran Excavación, en Moria.\
\
Deberías regresar con Fastarr para completar la mejora de tu arma.","El nido de arañas","¡Los enanos de la antigua armería han sido devorados!","'Sí, amigo mío, conozco un lugar donde se puede obtener la habilidad que buscas. Se trata de uan antigua armería que perteneció al linaje de mi propia familia. Sobre el yunque de su interior se forjaron muchas armas excelentes.\
\
'De hecho, ayer mismo envié una expedición de los míos para reclamar esta cámara sagrada, así que no debería haber ningún problema con que la uses... salvo, por supuesto, por el asunto de las tarifas y la compensación.\
\
'Sin embargo, antes de que siquiera consideres ir a la armería, debes traerme un diamante imbuido que yo pueda preparar para recibir dicha calidad. Por desgracia, no sabría decirte dónde encontrar uno.'","'Tendrás que traerme una adamantita imbuida para que podamos comenzar.'","'¡Ah, has sido capaz de encontrar un diamante imbuido! Te lo devolveré antes de que te dirijas a la armería.\
\
'Habla conmigo de nuevo cuando estés listo para partir.'","Lleva el diamante potenciado a Fastarr","'¿No has sido capaz de potenciar la piedra? Sin un diamante potenciado, no puedo ayudarte.'","Una antigua armería abandonada que perteneció a los antepasados de Fastarr alberga un yunque que sería idóneo para otorgar la habilidad que buscas para tu arma. Ya se ha enviado una expedición de enanos para segurarla.","'¿Sigues entero? Excelente. Y lo que es mejor: ¡has potenciado la piedra! Bien hecho, de verdad.\
\
'Entrégame ese diamante y veremos si podemos otorgarle la calidad que deseas.'","'¡No sé cómo agradecerte que hayas rescatado a mis parientes del nido de arañas! Que tu barba crezca cada vez más... bueno, si es que tienes una...'","Habla con Fastarr para viajar al nido de arañas","'¡Ah!¡Terribles noticias, ${PLAYER}! Un mensajero acaba de regresar de la armería...¡mis parientes han sido capturados! Dice que la expedición tropezó con un horrible nido de arañas malignas dentro de la armería.¡Serán devorados sin remedio si nadie los rescata!\
\
'Por favor, ${PLAYER}, te lo ruego: ve tan rápido como puedas y rescata a mis parientes de las arañas! A cambio, podrás hacer uso de lo que desees de la forja y las herramientas de mis antepasados...¡Pero date prisa antes de que sea demasiado tarde!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no se puede completar en una hermandad.</rgb>","Lleva un diamante imbuido a Fastarr","Fastarr te ha pedido que le traigas un diamante imbuido que él pueda preparar para otorgar una calidad a tu arma. Desafortunadamente, no sabe dónde se puede encontrar una piedra así."},
[13070]={"Todos los días hay algo que hacer durante el Festival de Primavera. ¡Únete a todo el mundo y participa en las diversas actividades del Festival de Primavera durante cuatro días!","'¡Te doy la bienvenida, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}!\
\
'Si estás aquí por el Festival de Primavera, te recomiendo que eches un vistazo y participes en todas estas actividades tan divertidas que hay por aquí. Y si no estás aquí por el Festival de Primavera, ¡tal vez deberías estarlo!\
\
'Para aquellas personas que participen en muchas de nuestras actividades, podría haber una recompensa aguardando, ¡así que sal ahí fuera!\
\
'Y recuerda: ¡si te pierdes en el laberinto de setos, simplemente pide ayuda a gritos!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Nota: Esta misión no puede cancelarse y se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando termine el festival actual.</rgb>","¡Hay mucho que hacer durante el Festival de Primavera! ¡Participa a menudo para ganar regalos maravillosos!\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>(Hay recompensas por participar en actividades durante doce días en 'Una primavera ajetreada' y 'Sabor a primavera'. ¡Planifícate en consecuencia! Estas misiones se eliminarán de tu registro de misiones cuando termine el festival actual.)</rgb>","'¡Hay que ver, ${PLAYER}, sí que te gusta la primavera, ¿no? Doce días de jolgorio no es poca cosa.\
\
'¡Has marcado una gran diferencia aquí, de veras! ¡Vuelve el año que viene, cuando tendré nuevos regalos listos para ti!'","Completa 'Una primavera ajetreada (intermedio)'","You have participated in Spring Festival activities for twelve days! You should talk to either Sergeant Tom at the Bree-land Festival Grounds or TBD near the Stable-master in Clegur.","Completa 'Una primavera ajetreada (introducción)'","'¡Vaya, vaya, ${PLAYER}, has hecho un trabajo excelente! ¡Doce días enteros!\
\
¡Todo tu duro trabajo ha ayudado a que el festival salga a pedir de boca! ¡Espero verte el año que viene, cuando tendré nuevos regalos listos para ti!'","'¡Te doy la bienvenida, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}!\
\
'¿Estás aquí por los Días de los Narcisos? Si es así, deberías hablar con Athra Devister, que está justo ahí. Si no estás aquí por los Días de los Narcisos, has llegado en buen momento para apreciar nuestros narcisos.'\
\
'Para aquellas personas que se unan a la diversión, podría haber un regalito aguardando, ¡si entiendes lo que quiero decir!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Nota: Esta misión no puede cancelarse y se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando termine el festival actual.</rgb>","Todos los días hay algo que hacer durante el Festival de Primavera. ¡Únete a todo el mundo y participa en las muchas actividades del Festival de Primavera durante cuatro días más!","Completa 'Una primavera ajetreada (final)'","Habla con el sargento Tom","El esplendor de la primavera","Talk to TBD","Todos los días hay algo que hacer durante el Festival de Primavera. ¡Únete a todo el mundo y participa en las diversas actividades del Festival de Primavera durante cuatro días más!"},
[13071]={"Thama Aklam has many coffers in it, likely home to ill-gotten gains.","Discover the camp of Thama Aklam","You have inspected many coffers.","At first glance, the chest appears empty, but a seasoned adventurer knows that looks can be deceiving.\
\
You knock on the bottom of the chest. It rings hollow.\
\
Aha! A false bottom.\
\
You pry it open with your fingers to reveal a hidden compartment that is also...\
\
Empty.","The Spoils of Thama Aklam","Inspect coffers (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","You spy some coffers in Thama Aklam that are probably filled with ill-gotten gains.\
\
Investigate these coffers to see what has been keeping the brigands so busy.","Thama Aklam has become home to a number of brigands.","'After a thorough inspection of their coffers, you can safely conclude that these brigands are either largely inactive or largely ineffective.'","You open the chest, anticipating gold and glittering jewels, but are instead met with the sight and smell of an old, mouldy shirt.\
\
Why would anyone keep this?","Within this coffer is a small supply crate.\
\
You pry open the lid, revealing a strongbox.\
\
The strongbox, in turn, contains a thick canvas sack.\
\
You peer into the bag only to find a small chest.\
\
You open the chest, expecting to find something precious, something worth something to anyone, but it is empty.\
\
And then you realize, the containers were the real treasures all along.","Among the mundane items in this coffer, you find a stack of neatly folded papers.\
\
Perhaps these are missives, plans for attacking nearby settlements or travellers on the road.\
\
A cursory examination reveals them instead to be love letters -- poorly written love letters best not read by anyone. Ever.","Thama Aklam is host to many suspicious coffers.\
\
Inspect coffers in Thama Aklam."},
[13073]={"'Los crebain nos causarán menos problemas ahora que Pizumu está muerto.'","Derrota a Pizumu, maestro de espías","'Aunque has dado un duro golpe a los crebain, siguen persistiendo. Sus alas negras oscurecen el cielo día y noche.\
\
'He pasado muchos días contemplando la fuente de los crebain, porque aunque cada día se ven más volando hacia Eregion desde las Tierras Brunas y Fangorn, no se les ha visto volar de regreso ni una sola vez.\
\
'Deben estar reportándose a alguien en Eregion. Ve al norte y al este, por las carreteras que serpentean hacia la Puerta del Cuerno Rojo, y busca a este maestro espía. Una vez que se le haya tratado, tal vez tengamos algo de paz, y el cielo ya no llevará el sonido incesante de las alas de los cuervos.'","Pizumu, el maestro espía, se encuentra al noreste de Echad Dúnann, por la carretera que serpentea hacia la Puerta del Cuerno Rojo.\
\
Authlanc te ha pedido que elimines al maestro espía de Saruman.","Authlanc está en Echad Dúnann, al suroeste de la Puerta del Cuerno Rojo.\
\
Debes regresar a Authlanc e informarle de tu éxito.","Habla con Authlanc en Echad Dúnann","El maestro espía","Has eliminado a muchos crebain en la Puerta del Cuerno Rojo, pero Authlanc teme que los pájaros estén guiados por una amenaza más inmediata.","'¿El maestro espía ha muerto? Todos podremos dormir más tranquilos sin el miedo a las alas batiendo y los picos afilados.\
\
'Te doy las gracias, ${PLAYER}.'","Pizumu, maestro espía, derrotado","'El maestro espía debería estar al noreste de Echad Dúnann, por la carretera que serpentea hacia la Puerta del Cuerno Rojo.'"},
[13076]={"There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.","Bring the Tokens of Hytbold to Egmund","The Stable: Entwash Vale Horses","Gather Tokens of Hytbold (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Our stable is ready for horses to come and fill it. There are many horses out there upon the plains which have been trained and groomed for a variety of tasks and jobs. Each area of the Eastemnet has their own section of expertise. We should bring in horses trained by each of these areas.'","'Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'"},
[13077]={"There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.","Bring the Tokens of Hytbold to Segwine","Gather Tokens of Hytbold (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Our stable is ready for horses to come and fill it. There are many horses out there upon the plains which have been trained and groomed for a variety of tasks and jobs. Each area of the Eastemnet has their own section of expertise. We should bring in horses trained by each of these areas.'","'Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'","The Stable: Norcrofts Horses"},
[13079]={"There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.","The Stable: Sutcrofts Horses","Gather Tokens of Hytbold (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring the Tokens of Hytbold to Harsterre","'Our stable is ready for horses to come and fill it. There are many horses out there upon the plains which have been trained and groomed for a variety of tasks and jobs. Each area of the Eastemnet has their own section of expertise. We should bring in horses trained by each of these areas.'","'Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'"},
[13080]={"There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.","The Stable: Wold Horses","Gather Tokens of Hytbold (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Our stable is ready for horses to come and fill it. There are many horses out there upon the plains which have been trained and groomed for a variety of tasks and jobs. Each area of the Eastemnet has their own section of expertise. We should bring in horses trained by each of these areas.'","'Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'","Bring the Tokens of Hytbold to Hargar"},
[13081]={"Talk to Yared","Collect the pivotal crate","Collected the pivotal crate","Make your way to the top of Yared's stack of crates and set the pivotal crate there to win The Stacking Game.","The Stacking Game","'This is the pivotal crate, my friend. I need it placed atop the northernmost stack, and if you can manage it then we win! Otherwise, the height of the stacks remains unchanged and we lose... as usual!'","Yared is waiting for you below.","Yared has asked you to pick up the pivotal crate and attempt to win The Stacking Game.","'Now climb up there and win The Stacking Game for us!'","Win the Stacking Game by placing the pivotal crate at the winning spot","Yared is engaged in a contest with some others of his folk, and he is very worried that without your help he will lose.","'Very nicely done, my friend! You must tell me your name. ${PLAYER}? I see. It is good to meet you, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'I know this is just a silly game, and we should not let it affect us so much as it does... but there was little else for us to do once Hámisar shut the gates. Now that visitors are coming once again to Furukzahar, perhaps there will be less need for us to play the Stacking Game.\
\
'Thank you again for helping us to win, my new friend! Winning is not everything, of course, but it happens to me so rarely that I must cherish it when it does!'","Cheers (and a few groans) erupt from below as you win The Stacking Game for Yared's team","'You! You there! You look like you might be the sort who hungers for adventure! You must always be climbing about the wilderness, scaling cliffs and leaping from dangerous embankments, yes?'\
\
You tell the dwarf that you have been known to do some of those things from time to time.\
\
'I need your help! You see, we are engaged in a little friendly competition to see which team of dwarves can stack their pile of crates the highest. We call it The Stacking Game, and it is something we came to play in the weeks following the outbreak of war in Gondor, when Hámisar ordered shut the gates of Furukzahar. My team only has two members on it, and we are losing... just as we lost the game before, and the game before that! But since the other team has three... you are free to join us!\
\
'This is the pivotal crate, my friend. I need it placed atop the northernmost stack, and if you can manage it then we win! Otherwise, the height of the stacks remains unchanged and we lose... as usual!'"},
[13082]={"You have collected a vicious-looking spear, its point tipped with old blood","'Tonight is the Feast of the Running Stag, our clan's annual festival. It is an important ritual, and you must join us and share our fare. Tonight, you are of the Caru-lûth, the Stag-clan!\
\
'Now, be off with you! I must prepare, and I cannot remember where I left the three ritual pieces... curse this old head of mine!\
\
'The crown, the spear, the hair... where did I leave them...?'","You hold in your hands a lock of hair from the tail of a horse","Find the third piece of the ritual set","Bring the pieces of the ritual set to Elder Riagán","The items for the ritual feast can be found somewhere in Lhan Tarren.\
\
You should help Elder Riagán find the items that he has lost, for they will be needed tonight at the feast, and it seems as though his old mind has forgotten their whereabouts.","Find the second piece of the ritual set","You have picked up a crudely-hewn crown made of sticks and rocks","Find the first piece of the ritual set","'Oh! You are a kind one, ${PLAYER}. I am ready to replace the rest of the Stag-clan with just you, if truth be told. Ha!\
\
'Do not pay me any mind. They are a useless, little clan, but they are no less dear to me for that.\
\
'Thank you for helping an old man gather his wits. Now I may begin to prepare for tonight.'","The Stag-clan of Trum Dreng","'It was not always so difficult for me to remember where I left things. My poor, old head!'","You have passed into Dunland and now find yourself welcomed into the homes of the simple folk of Lhan Tarren, a small village inhabited by the Caru-lûth, the Stag-clan.","Elder Riagán can be found in Lhan Tarren, musing over the whereabouts of the items you found.\
\
You should bring the pieces of the ritual set to Elder Riagán for tonight's feast."},
[13083]={"Find evidence of Old Skárhogg's presence at Skelstrand","Examine the slain Angmarim","'Do you remember how I told you that the ukhrâsh chased me off at Skelstrand? Well, the last time I was run off, I got lucky. I was ambushed by an enormous ukhrash, and it was very nearly upon me before I finally heard it. If I had reacted a second later, well... it would have been worse than this!'\
\
Orti pulls back his sleeve to reveal a thin gash on his arm.\
\
'And that was the smallest scratch, mind you! If it had been closer, I surely would have lost my arm. Aye, it's a sneaky one. Especially for one of its size!\
\
'Old Skárhogg, as I call it, has grown a bit too long in the claw, I think. If it is allowed to stalk the banks of Durthuzâram, there is no doubt in my mind that it will endanger the dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ.\
\
'If you go to Skelstrand, seek out some sign of its presence. I only hope that you find it before it finds you!'","A sudden bubbling and clattering heralds the arrival of Old Skárhogg","Old Skárhogg might be found stalking the waters around Skelstrand.\
\
You have discovered an Angmarim slain by a massive ukhrash, likely Old Skárhogg. You should remain alert and defeat Old Skárhogg.","You find a slain Angmarim marked with wounds alike the claws of an ukhrash","'You found Old Skárhogg, didn't you? I see it on your face. Well, what happened?'\
\
You tell Orti that you managed to defeat Old Skárhogg, but that it had apparently also slain one of the Angmarim of the Iron Crown that drew too near its lair.\
\
'What could those Men possibly want with the ukhrash? Bah, perhaps they just saw the same shimmering in the lake that I did and simply couldn't resist. It's a pity that Old Skárhogg didn't slay more of them, but I am certain our luck would have run out sooner or later!\
\
'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.'","The Stalker of Skelstrand","Old Skárhogg falls defeated!","Talk to Orti","Orti can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn.\
\
Although it seemingly posed an equally dire threat to the Iron Crown in Gloomingtarn, you have defeated Old Skárhogg and made the western banks of Durthuzâram safe once again. You should return to Orti.","Old Skárhogg might be found stalking the waters around Skelstrand.\
\
Orti has asked you to find evidence of Old Skárhogg's presence at Skelstrand and put an end to the dangerous ukhrash before it can hinder the Gabil'akkâ in Gloomingtarn.","After narrowly escaping a massive ukhrash at Skelstrand, Orti fears that the ukhrash, Old Skárhogg, may pose a threat to the Gabil'akkâ and any who seek to pass through Gloomingtarn."},
[13084]={"'Get away from us! We only talk to one man and you are not him!\
\
'Go away!'","'It was a boy? I was talking with a boy and not a crow? I do not believe you! I will have to talk this over with my friend, the Orc-mouse, to see what he thinks.\
\
'Or was it a crow?\
\
'Thank you for naught, and a good day to you.'","'They all think that I am mad because I talk to a crow...but it truly talks, I tell you! I did not believe it myself at first, but we have spoken many times, and it speaks as well as you and I.\
\
'Did you hear that? Just over....\
\
'I heard it with my own two ears, but...I would indeed feel better if someone else would speak with it, as well. Would you speak with the mouse? Or was it an Orc? Oh, yes, the crow.'","'How did you know it was me? I have been fooling that mad old man for weeks now!\
\
'Please do not tell anyone. I will be in terrible trouble. I will stop pestering Bertred...I promise.'","The squawking of a nearby crow catches your attention","Bertred has been having conversations with a crow, lending to the impression others have that he is mad.","The talking crow is in the western part of Aldburg.\
\
Bertred asked to to attempt to speak with the talking crow.","The Stalking Squawk","Bertred is at his home in Aldburg.\
\
The decision lies with you: speak with the child and let him go or speak with Bertred and bring the wrath of the mad Quartermaster down upon the child.","'You are not going to tell anyone? I promise not to do it ever again. I will be good...I swear it!'","Talk to Bertred","There is a child hiding behind the bush near the crow.\
\
You should speak with the child.","Talk to the meddling child","You notice a rustling behind a nearby bush","Find the talking crow","The crow was last seen in the western portion of Aldburg.\
\
Bertred wants you to find his talking crow and attempt to speak with it in order to prove that he is not mad.","Speak with the talking crow"},
[13085]={"La Piedra Erguida se desbloquea. ¡Recoge tu recompensa rápidamente!","Recibe tu recompensa de la Piedra Erguida","¡Has desvelado el misterio de la Piedra Erguida!","<rgb=#FF0000>Completa el ritual, ¡rápido!</rgb>","Ves un texto garabateado en la piedra. Dice:\
\
'Acércate. El ritual para desbloquear mi botín es el siguiente:\
\
'John,\
'Marla Shelton,\
'Sargento de armas Irminric,\
'Bragi Mazorroca,\
'Gapi.'","La Piedra Erguida","Desbloquea la piedra erguida para recibir tu recompensa.","El ritual fue incorrecto","Has encontrado una piedra erguida misteriosa.","Recoge tu recompensa de la Piedra Erguida"},
[13086]={"Deberías llevar el liquen que recogiste a Hafren.\
\
Hafren está en el convoy de Gerwyn, en el norte de Cardolan.","Vuelve con Hafren","Las piedras erguidas de Tyrn Gorthad","'Te doy las gracias. Has ayudado a salvar las vidas de mis compañeros y prolongado la vida de las piedras también.'","'Uno de nuestros exploradores regresó con informes de grandes círculos de piedras erguidas al otro lado de la colina cruzando el camino.\
\
'Si te encuentras entre ellas, ¿podrías buscar un liquen gris verdoso que pueda estar creciendo en sus superficies? Tiene poderes curativos, y también destruye lentamente las piedras. ¡Ráscalo suavemente y tráelo aquí para recibir una recompensa!'","Hafren te ha pedido que recojas liquen de las piedras erguidas.\
\
Las piedras erguidas se encuentran en Tyrn Gorthad.","Las piedras erguidas de Tyrn Gorthad están cubiertas con un liquen de lenta expansión.","Recoge liquen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Liquen recogido (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[13087]={"Lleva la piedra élfica a la piedra erguida y vence a su guardián","'Has hecho bien en derrotar al señor de los montículos, ${PLAYER}. Muy bien hecho.'","'Lleva la piedra élfica a la tumba del señor de los montículos, entre las tumbas de los Edain, al noreste de aquí.'","'Seres reanimados rondan las tumbas de Haudh Lin. No sé qué presagia esto, ya que nunca antes se habían visto tales criaturas en estas tierras. Son las criaturas del Rey Brujo de Angmar. Esto no augura nada bueno para Eriador y quizás para toda la Tierra Media, ya que los ojos que deberían estar mirando al sur podrían volverse hacia el norte y perder de vista la amenaza mayor.\
\
'Como siempre ocurre con el mal, sin duda una voluntad mayor guía a las menores entre las tumbas. Es esa voluntad mayor la que debe ser destruida. Solo así se verán obstaculizados los designios de Angmar para Ered Luin.\
\
'Lleva esta piedra élfica a las tumbas y colócala sobre la piedra erguida más grande. Es una piedra blanca cerca de un edificio en ruinas. La piedra élfica posee tal virtud que podría hacer que esa voluntad mayor de la que hablé se manifestara, y tú debes enfrentarte a ella.'","Derrotado el Señor de los montículos","Nada sucede","Presenta la piedra élfica en la piedra erguida","Los tumularios rondan las antiguas tumbas de los Edain, en los confines orientales de Haudh Lin, anunciando la llegada de un gran mal a Ered Luin.","La piedra erguida blanca se encuentra entre las antiguas tumbas de los Edain, al noreste de la casa de Glamir, cerca de las ruinas de un viejo edificio.\
\
Glamir te ha dicho que lleves la piedra élfica a las tumbas de los Edain y la coloques sobre la piedra erguida más grande. Cree que la criatura cuya voluntad gobierna a los seres reanimados de Haudh Lin podría ser atraída por su presencia.","Vence al Señor de los montículos","'Bien hecho. Estos tontos enanos podrían haberse topado con algo que no podrían esperar derrotar si no hubieras intervenido antes de que el mal reuniera sus fuerzas. Esas tierras malditas seguirán siendo oscuras y encantadas, pero se puede esperar que ya no representen una amenaza inmediata.'","Glamir se encuentra dentro de las ruinas, al suroeste de las antiguas tumbas de los Edain.\
\
Tal como predijo Glamir, la piedra élfica atrajo al amo de los seres reanimados. Deberías volver a ver a Glamir para contarle tu victoria sobre la criatura.","'Es triste que la tierra de mi hogar esté manchada por el terror de Angmar.'","La piedra erguida","'¿Dónde está mi piedra élfica?'","La piedra élfica verde brilla en tu mano.","Lleva la piedra élfica a Glamír"},
[13088]={"'¡Ven conmigo. ¡La Corona de Durin nos espera!'","Ayuda a Byrski Proadura a contruir un barco","¡Obra maestra!","'¡Creo que con eso bastará! Ahora bien, ¿por qué no haces los honores? No, no, insisto.\
\
¡Eres ${PLAYERNAME:un Marinero[m]|una Marinera[f]} hábil, después de todo! Estoy seguro de que puedes construir un barco adecuado para nuestra expedición.\
\
Bueno entonces, me haré a un lado y te dejaré trabajar!'","El Favor de las Estrellas","Derrota a orcos en Uruk-gashan, en el Valle del Arroyo Sombrío (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL}).","Byrski Hardprow se encuentra en Mekhem-bizru en el Valle del Arroyo Sombrío.\
\
Lo has ayudado a presenciar la Corona de Durin en el Lago Espejo. Debes hablar con Byrski Proadura.","Recolecta tablas de madera de acebo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Debes ayudar a Byrski Proadura a construir un barco para su expedición.","Tablas de madera de acebo recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Byrski Proadura","Byrski Proadura se encuentra en Mekhem-bizru en el Valle del Arroyo Sombrío.\
\
Has construido con éxito un barco adecuado para tu expedición al Lago Espejo. Debes hablar con Byrski Proadura.","Debes ayudar a Byrski Proadura a construir un barco para su expedición, pero quizá esta vez deberías esforzarte un poco más.","Ayuda a Byrski a construir un barco digno de presenciar la Corona de Durin","'Sin embargo, hay un pequeño problema, mi ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Después de todo, ¡no podría navegar un barco a través de toda Moria!\
\
He preparado algunos diseños para construir un barco, pero me faltan ciertos materiales que necesito. Por desgracia, esos orcos cerca de la Piedra de Durin —lo irrespetuosos que son— están en posesión de mis tablas de madera de acebo. ¿Por qué no los ahuyentas y recoges parte de esa madera? Una vez que eso esté hecho, creo que tendremos todas las herramientas necesarias para construir un barco, y mucho menos de qué preocuparnos cuando estemos en el Lago Espejo. ¡Después de todo, no queremos que una flecha orca perdida atraviese nuestras velas!\
\
¡Vamos, mi ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. No hay tiempo que perder!'","Los orcos y las tablas de madera de Iles puede encontrarse en Uruk-gashan, en el Valle del Arroyo Sombrío.\
\
Byrski Proadura te ha pedido ahuyentar a los orcos que acechan en el valle y recolectar tablas de madera de acebo.","Entrega las tablas de madera de acebo a Byrski Proadura en Mekhem-bizru.","Orcos derrotados en Uruk-gashan en el Valle del Arroyo Sombrío (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Bah! Tienes que pensar un poco más en grande. ¡Vamos a una expedición, no a un día de pesca!\
\
Inténtalo de nuevo, ${PLAYER}. ¡Necesito un barco digno de presenciar la Corona de Durin!'","Byrski Proadura se encuentra en Mekhem-bizru en el Valle del Arroyo Sombrío.\
\
Has recogido varias tablas de madera de acebo y ahuyentado a muchos orcos en Uruk-gashan. Debes regresar con Byrski Proadura.","'¡Ja-ja! ¡Ahora sí que me gusta!\
\
Y bien, vayamos al Lago Espejo. Si necesitas prepararte, tómate el tiempo que necesites, ¡pero no me hagas esperar!'","¿Quizás se veía mejor en tu cabeza?","Byrski Proadura se encuentra en Mekhem-bizru en el Valle del Arroyo Sombrío.","'Bueno, creo que al menos vi la Corona de Durin, ¡así que Brogur se alegrará de oírlo! Aunque quizá deberías preguntarles a los Elfos sobre lo que viste.\
\
De cualquier modo, te agradezco tu ayuda. Le has prestado un gran servicio a la Guarnición de Hierro, y me aseguraré de que Brogur —y Bósi, por supuesto— sepan ${PLAYERNAME:del Marinero[m]|de la Marinera[f]} que nos permitió encontrar la Corona de Durin. ¡Ojalá eso signifique que la reclamación de Khazad-dûm pronto llegará a su fin!'","Byrski Proadura se ha ofrecido a buscar la Corona de Durin en el Lago Espejo, con la esperanza de que anuncie un final auspicioso para la reclamación de Khazad-dûm por parte de la Guarnición de Hierro."},
[13089]={"Assist with affairs in Thornholt","Assist at Stormwall","Talk to Stráhek the Stout","The State of the Expedition","Help out in all major affairs in the Dwarf-holds, including: 'Into the Ironfold', 'An Audience with the Boy King', 'An Unexpected Story', 'Scars of Battle', 'Across the Chasm', 'In the Halls of Thikil-gundu', and 'Etterfang.'","Stráhek can be found in Skarháld in the Grey Mountains.\
\
You should talk with Stráhek the Stout about the Zhélruka efforts to establish themselves in the Grey Mountains.","'Ah, there is always more to do. They say the work of the dwarves is never done, and that is as true today as it was in days past! Explore the lands of the dwarves and see their travails through to their conclusion! I do not doubt further adventures await in the Ironfold and Ered Mithrin.'","Help out in all major affairs in the Dwarf-holds.","Assist in the Steel Keep","There is much to do in the Dwarf-holds, after all is said and done.","Complete each of the major story-lines for the Dwarf-holds","Follow Nori's trail","Assist Náin with Hammerstead and Utterby","Assist in the Glimmerdeep mines","Complete 'Into the Ironfold'","'You again, ${CLASS}. I will not lie. It has been hard going, here in the Grey Mountains. Hard going even for a people that has come thousands of perilous, wearying leagues.\
\
'Still, we dwarves are hardy folk and will not be daunted. When pressed greatly, we will ask for help... especially of those who show themselves good of will and worthy to the task.\
\
'Will you assist us in our efforts? There is much, yes much to be done!'"},
[13090]={"'Thank you for your assistance, ${PLAYER}. Without your help, setting up an outpost here would have been much more difficult. And perhaps we would have sent aid supplies to goblins.'\
\
Nashôn's face momentarily flushes red before he clears his throat and resumes speaking.\
\
'Our work here will continue, but I will only ask one more thing of you. Belondor wants a report on how things are proceeding here at Kruha-sûrja. Would you mind speaking to him in Dâr Laja on our behalf? Thank you for all of your help ${PLAYER}.'","Nashôn has asked you to report to Belondor in Dâr Laja, the Meeting-hall in Umbar Baharbêl with news of the guards' progress in the sewers beneath the Sail-haven.","'${PLAYER}, you have returned. How goes the efforts in the sewers?'\
\
You tell Belondor of the efforts taken in the new guard post at Kruha-sûrja, and he nods.\
\
'Thank you for helping them get a head start while they work on setting up the outpost. Assuring the safety of the people of the Sail-haven will go a long way in restoring their confidence in the Kindred of the Coins.'","Talk to Belondor","You have helped the guards that Belondor sent to the sewers beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.","The State of the Sewers"},
[13091]={"Defeat the siege trolls assaulting Helm's monument (${VALUE}/5)","The statue of Helm has been destroyed","Helm Hammerhand's statue must be defended from the enemies seeking to desecrate his memorial and dishearten the soldiers guarding the dike.","The Statue of Helm Hammerhand","Helm Hammerhand's memorial stands upon the Dike at the location where he perished. The Rohirrim draw inspiration and courage from the sight of the statue raised above the trench wall. The enemy cannot be allowed to destroy the statue while the men of Rohan still stand to defend Helm's Dike.\
\
Merit Rating\
\
This quest starts with <rgb=#FFFF00>Full</rgb> Merit Rating.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Major Merit Loss:</rgb>\
* Statue is dealt heavy damage\
* Rohirrim guards defeated","<rgb=#FF0000>Do not allow Helm's statue to be destroyed</rgb>"},
[13094]={"The swarm catches the scent of honey!","'Hello and welcome to Bergraw! We produce Pinnath Gelin's prized Calengaran. Bottles were sent up to the table of the king and his lady themselves for the wedding! Have you tried it?\
\
'Yes, we pride ourselves on our wine, however this season's batches are in serious peril. So much has been going strangely lately on our Green Hills. Talk of goblins and Southrons. Something happened to Cornworth Farm and I haven't been able to get yeast from them for months! I've had to make due with yeast made from our very own grapes. It'll change the flavour, but will still be Bergraw worthy, of course. Only problem is, I can't get near the barrel the yeast is growing in to collect it! One bee sting could mean my death – my own gran had her throat close up because of it, many years back. We've all been careful since.\
\
'Maybe you can help. I have some honey to distract the bees with, but you'll have to be quick! Take up that honey there, bring it a distance away from the barrel of grape yeast, and then make a run for it! You should be able to gather yeast in time, before they get back. I'm… nearly sure of it!'","You should place the honeypot a ways away from the barrel of grapes.\
\
A good spot for the honeypot can be found at Bergraw in Pinnath Gelin.","Pick up the honey pot","Collect yeast","Collected yeast","'Whew, you hustled like a bee was in your britches for sure! Haha! Did you get the yeast then? Let's have it, shall we?'","Leithiel has asked you to distract a swarm of bees with some honey. You should pick up the jar of honey.\
\
The honey is next to Leithiel at Bergraw in Pinnath Gelin.","You should bring the yeast you've collected to Leithiel at her vineyard in Pinnath Gelin.","Place the honeypot","With local farms under various forms of attack, wine makers in Pinnath Gelin have had to become resourceful in their methods.","Bring the yeast to Leithiel","The Stinging Harvest"},
[13095]={"Gelirwen se encuentra en el Refugio Sombrío.\
\
Descubriste un objeto en el señor de Skûmfil. Es posible que la otra mitad del objeto repose en el otro combatiente del lugar.","'Es como pensaba: una protección utilizada para sellar una puerta. Si hay accesos dentro de Skûmfil, es posible que este objeto se usara para permitir el paso, a modo de llave.'","'El objeto que me has traído parece ser algún tipo de llave o protección, pero está partido. No puedo estar segura hasta que tengas ambas piezas. Regresa cuando hayas recuperado la segunda parte del objeto.'","Este fragmento, hallado sobre el rey kergrim, parece haber sido partido en dos. Es posible que este objeto pueda unirse con otro similar.\
\
Deberías encontrar la segunda mitad del objeto y mostrar ambas piezas a Gelirwen en el Refugio Sombrío.","Fragmento de la reina recogido (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","La protección pestilente","Recoge el fragmento de la reina (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","La protección pestilente, hallada rota sobre el cadáver del líder de Skûmfil, podría ser un medio para adentrarse en las profundidades del área plagada de kergrim e insectos.","Lleva los fragmentos a Gelirwen en el Refugio Sombrío"},
[13096]={"Recoge el fragmento del rey (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Este fragmento, hallado sobre la reina grodbog, parece haber sido partido en dos. Es posible que este objeto pueda unirse con otro similar.\
\
Deberías encontrar la segunda mitad del objeto y mostrar ambas piezas a Gelirwen en el Refugio Sombrío.","'El objeto que me has traído parece ser algún tipo de llave o protección, pero está partido. No puedo estar segura hasta que tengas ambas piezas. Regresa cuando hayas recuperado la segunda parte del objeto.'","La protección pestilente","Gelirwen se encuentra en el Refugio Sombrío.\
\
Descubriste un objeto en la reina grodbog de Skûmfil. Es posible que la otra mitad del objeto repose en el otro combatiente del lugar.","Fragmento del rey recogido (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva los fragmentos a Gelirwen en el Refugio Sombrío","'Es como pensaba: se trata de una protección utilizada para sellar una puerta. Si existen accesos de este tipo dentro de Skûmfil, es posible que este objeto se usara para permitir el paso.'","La protección pestilente, hallada partida sobre el cadáver del líder de Skûmfil, podría ser un medio para adentrarse en las profundidades del área plagada de kergrim e insectos."},
[13097]={"You have found the Narghâk workshop in Starkhaven","Talk to Corudan at the Narghâk workshop in Starkhaven","Bring the bottles of Narghâk to Corudan at the workshop in Starkhaven","This weapon is used to launch Narghâk through the air with explosive force","'Even a small quantity of Narghâk can inflict grievous harm! We must retrieve as many bottles of this deadly substance from the Heirsworn as we can.'","What did the engineer think to retrieve from the marked barrel by the Narghâk workshop?","Corudan has learned that Heirsworn Corsairs throughout Sûg Nidar may carry small glass bottles containing quantities of Narghâk.","Deprived Corsairs of Narghâk bottles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Corudan is concerned about the development of Narghâk weapons that might be used by the Song of Waves and Wind.","Plans nearby may describe the construction process for designing such Narghâk weapons as those located at the Starkhaven workshop. You should examine the plans and defeat any who try to stop you.","El Almacén","'The Song of Waves and Wind would be dangerous enough by itself, but Nakási has armed it with terrifying weapons. I know not for how long Khôltekh has been working in secret with her, but he had his eye upon the stockpile of Hungry Fire from the moment we discovered it within Ashâgir. Did he wait until you travelled into Mûr Ghala with Inkanûsh and Glorfindel to give the command to his underlings to transport the Narghâk to Sûg Nidar?\
\
'The timing no longer matters. What matters to us now is that we prevent the Song from being equipped with weapons capable of using the Hungry Fire against its enemies. There must be a workshop of some kind within Starkhaven where such weapons can be assembled. Let us search for it among the buildings of Starkhaven on the western shore of the Fearwater. If we can destroy the Narghâk stockpile these weapons will stand empty and unused.'","An engineer of Ordâkh bellows with rage and attacks!","The barrel is empty, but there are traces of Narghâk smeared at the bottom","'I have made an unpleasant discovery, friend. While I searched for the Narghâk stockpile, I was surprised by a number of Heirsworn Corsairs and it came to fighting. But they were not content to engage in combat with their blades alone, and they threw glass jars containing a small quantity of an oily substance at me.\
\
'I evaded this attack with little difficulty; am I not an Elf of Lórien? But when the jar shattered upon the ground it exploded with blue flame.\
\
'Some of Balakhâd's Corsairs have been given jars of Narghâk to use in battle, ${PLAYER}. We must retrieve these jars from them. Afterwards let us meet back here.'","Examine the plans for the Narghâk weapons intended for use by the Song, and defeat anyone who tries to stop you","'Did you separate the bottles of Narghâk from their bearers? Good, for I have done the same. I also found a stack of parchment within an encampment of the Ordâkhai. I think the soldiers knew not what to make of these papers. They are yellowed with age, and when we have finished here I will take some time to study them.\
\
'We found not the stockpile we sought, but I think we discovered the reason for that: the Hungry Fire has already been loaded onto the ships of the Song, and any excess considered unnecessary for their siphons and cannons have been given to the Heirsworn.\
\
'It is more necessary than ever that we prevent the Song from setting sail. May Cúridwan have the time she needs to distribute the blight among the vessels of the fleet, and may we capture or kill the ones who might give the command to sail! But for now we have done what we can.'","'The workshop for constructing the Narghâk weapons must be located among the buildings of Starkhaven on the western shore of the Fearwater. If we can destroy the Narghâk stockpile these weapons will stand empty and unused.'","Deprive Corsairs in Sûg Nidar of Narghâk bottles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The engineer perishes attempting to reach a nearby marked barrel","You should examine one of the unusual-looking weapons at the Narghâk workshop on the western shore of the Fearwater, in Starkhaven.","Corudan waits for word of your success at the Narghâk workshop on the western shore of the Fearwater, in Starkhaven.","Find the Narghâk workshop in Starkhaven, on the western shore of the Fearwater","This barrel is also empty of Narghâk. As you stand up, Corudan arrives","Examine another marked barrel by the Narghâk workshop","Examine the marked barrel by the Narghâk workshop","Corudan wants to search for the Narghâk workshop he believes to be located somewhere among the buildings on the western shore of the Fearwater, in Starkhaven.","Examine one of the unusual-looking weapons at the Narghâk workshop","Corudan has come to the Narghâk workshop at Starkhaven."},
[13098]={"'I am glad you have returned, but Odahild wishes to speak with you first. I cannot blame her, for she has become impatient with us. It seems that speaking in hushed tones and whispers does not cause people to trust you, ${PLAYER}, did you know that?\
\
'Well, tell her what you have accomplished for the people of Blómgard. I trust she will be more satisfied if she is kept up to date with our progress.'","Côs Braen can be found in the southern edge of Laerlad.\
\
You should defeat those you find in Côs Braen.","The Ungoledan presence is most visible, and it darkens the wood","'Once there was a group of Men who respected the land and nature, and saw the beauty of the mountains and the vales between them. I was unlike them, of course, being a Wizard, but I did see some of myself in them. More than a little! I gave them a gift: the gift of skin-changing. I taught them how to use it, and as they practiced the art they became closer to nature, and I was most glad for them. They were a good people, and they remained so to this day: the Beornings of the Vales of Anduin.\
\
'But other Men became jealous of the gift. They captured one of the skin-changers, and tortured him, and in the end he gave away the secret art. These evil ones were driven mad by this new power, a power they were never intended to wield. These were the Gauredain, men of the wolf, and the Ungoledain, men of the spider.\
\
'I should have been more careful, ${PLAYER}. I repented of the gift, for once it was stolen I could do nothing. Now the Woodmen face a peril of my own creation. We must find their encampment and protect them from the leader of the Ungoledain. Mengris Tásakh, did they call it?'","Radagast can be found in Blómgard.\
\
You should talk to Radagast.","Destroy vile spider totems (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Ungoledain at Côs Braen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Regretting the allowance of skin-changing secrets falling into the wrong hands, Radagast seeks to end the Ungoledain presence in Laerlad for good.","Habla con Radagast","Seek out the Ungoledan encampment in Laerlad","'Odahild believes your arrival was a good portent? Ha! Perhaps it was. I am glad she is pleased with our efforts. Now I have some pressing matters to discuss with you concerning my home. I speak of Rhosgobel.'","Odahild can be found in Blómgard.\
\
You should talk to Odahild.","'So this Ungoledan encampment has been destroyed? Good. I felt the air change when you first entered the village, and although I did not know it at the time it truly must have been a good omen. I hope that you have done enough to persuade these beasts to never set foot in our woods again, and if you have not, that you will continue to persuade them until they do!'","Destroyed vile spider totems (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Stolen Gift","Côs Braen can be found in the southern edge of Laerlad.\
\
You should seek out the Ungoledan encampment of Côs Braen in Laerlad.","Defeat spiders at Côs Braen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Arañas vencidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Ungoledain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Odahild"},
[13100]={"Recolecta el adorno roto","Gurmagath tiene en su poder un adorno que perteneció a Lachenn, Maestro de Lin Giliath.","'¿Todavía no has encontrado el adorno de Lachenn? ¡No se puede permitir que Gurmagath lo conserve, ${PLAYER}!'","Lleva el adorno roto a Thaliollang","Gurmagath se encuentra en una loma en la zona noreste de Taur Gonwaith, al sureste de Lin Giliath.\
\
Thaliollang te pidió, en memoria de Lachenn, que cazases al caudillo de los trolls de piedra, Gurmagath, y recuperases el adorno de Lachenn para devolverlo a un lugar de honor.","'Gurmagath se encuentra en una elevación en la parte noreste de Taur Gonwaith. No se le puede permitir conservar el adorno de Lachenn por más tiempo, ${PLAYER}. Debes derrotarlo y llevarlo a Lin Giliath, donde pertenece.'","'He oído susurros entre los árboles sobre un caudillo troll de piedra de gran tamaño, llamado por los otros Gurmagath. ¡Este Gurmagath tenía en su gran puño un reluciente adorno que una vez perteneció al pobre Lachenn!\
\
'Esta miserable criatura no puede conservar el adorno de Lachenn, ${PLAYER}. Busca a Gurmagath y arrebátale el adorno de Lachenn, para que pueda guardarse en Lin Giliath en un lugar de honor.'","Thaliollang está en Lin Giliath, al noroeste de Taur Gonwaith.\
\
Thaliollang espera tu regreso con el adorno que recuperaste de Gurmagath.","El adorno robado","Adorno roto recolectado","'Sí, este es el adorno de Lachenn. Es una verdadera lástima que haya sido roto por los brutales dedos de Gurmagath.\
\
'Hay algo extraño en estas marcas en la parte trasera del adorno. Estos arañazos casi parecen formar letras. A... N... G...\
\
'El resto está roto, pero creo que sé lo que diría.'"},
[13101]={"'¿Estás... aquí para ayudar? ¡Ten cuidado! Un poderoso rascacueva ha matado... al resto de mi...'\
\
El enano tiembla de agotamiento.\
\
'Ese monstruoso rascacueva... nos atacó... después de que los trolls robaran... las piedras que... llevábamos...'","Habla con Tóki Barbablanca","Las Piedras Robadas","Los rascacuevas infestan las ruinas de Ost Dúrgonn, al norte del camino y del campamento de Barachen.\
\
Heithur Puñohierro cree que los rascacuevas de Ost Dúrgonn podrían haberse llevado las piedras y quizás atacaron con tal fuerza que lograron derrotar a los enanos.","'Claramente, la desgracia cayó sobre mis compañeros. Mis enanos pueden estar perdidos ahora, pero las piedras que escoltaban pueden recuperarse de quien sea o lo que sea que las haya robado. Esto debemos hacerlo, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Mientras regresaba del campamento de Glóin para reunirme con mis compañeros, vi una gran cantidad de rascacuevas a lo largo del camino, especialmente al norte del camino. Barachen me dice que las ruinas de Ost Dúrgonn también están cerca de allí... la antigua fortaleza de Rhudaur atraería criaturas como los rascacuevas, pues esas alimañas devoran piedra. Puede que la furia que los ha sacado de sus cuevas también los haya llevado a atacar caravanas armadas. Ay, las piedras robadas serían justo el tipo de botín que podría hacer que los rascacuevas se aglomeren así.\
\
'¿Investigarías Ost Dúrgonn en busca de alguna señal de las piedras? Como ocurre con muchas bestias, a menudo el líder de la manada guarda los bocados más preciados, y estas piedras sin duda lo serían. Quizás aún sobrevivan dentro de su inmunda guarida.'","Busca las piedras robadas en Ost Dúrgonn","¡Has defendido con éxito a Tóki Barbablanca!","'Muchas... gracias, buen ${RACE}. No creo... que hubiera podido resistir... mucho más.\
\
'¿Dices que Heithur Puñohierro... se ha refugiado con un... Elfo al sur de aquí? Iré... con él... entonces, cuando haya descansado un momento. Por favor... rastrea a los trolls que... robaron las piedras. Nos guiaron hasta aquí... pero creo que su campamento... está más al este, siguiendo el camino...'","Heithur Puñohierro está en el campamento de Barachen, al este del Último Puente y al sur del camino, en una colina inclinada bajo la sombra de altos acantilados.\
\
Has sabido por Tóki Barbablanca que las piedras que su compañía transportaba fueron robadas por trolls, aparentemente con ayuda del monstruoso rascacueva que derrotaste.","Los enanos de la compañía de Heithur Puñohierro han sufrido una desgracia cerca del Último Puente, y las piedras que transportaban para Glóin en Rivendel se han perdido."},
[13102]={"In an act of brashness, the scout Einar has lost his sword to an Angmarim.","The Stolen Sword","Draw out and defeat Akhún","You have reclaimed Einar's sword.\
\
You should return it to its rightful owner at Drenghól.","'At your service, ${PLAYER}... or I would be, if that blasted Angmarim hadn't stabbed me with my own blade.\
\
'Urgh... apologies. I got too close to a group of Angmarim while scouting, thinking they'd never catch me. Well, they dragged me to Dûn Traikh. Then one of them claimed my sword -- forged by my own mother -- for himself!\
\
'But I'm in no state to challenge him. If you're planning to head west and enter the camp, find the quartermaster, Akhún. He's rather irritable when his fellow Angmarim try to take weapons without his permission. Make enough noise with those weapons, and he'll come running!'","Dûn Traikh lies west of Drenghól.\
\
Einar suggested meddling with the Angmarim weapon stores to draw Akhún out so that you can reclaim his sword.","Found Einar's sword","'Ah... thank you, ${PLAYER}. I don't think I could have lived with myself, knowing that Akhún would've drawn the blood of my people using my mother's blade.\
\
'Maybe I'll live to see the day when I can put down this sword for good. But until then, I'll be more cautious.'","Deliver the sword to Einar"},
[13103]={"Las musarañas molestas se encuentran en el centro del Jardín del Festival de Duillond, y las botas para pisotearlas están en tu inventario.\
\
Debes localizar las botas en tu inventario y asignarlas como habilidad. Estas botas pueden usarse para pisotear a las musarañas que infestan el jardín. Cuando lo hagas, espera en el centro del jardín a que comience el juego de musarañas.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Para asignar las botas como habilidad, arrastra el objeto 'Botas de Poder Imaginable' desde tu inventario a tu barra de habilidades.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Las musarañas molestas son inmunes a cualquier otro ataque o maniobra ofensiva.</rgb>","'¡Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}! Es un comienzo. Pronto comenzará un nuevo juego; espero que participes también en el siguiente.'","'Deberás colocarte en el centro del jardín de abajo si deseas atrapar a las musarañas molestas.'","Asigna las botas para pisotear musarañas a tu barra de habilidades y espera el ataque","Toma las botas para pisotear musarañas de la caja cercana","Derrota musarañas antes de que termine la ronda","'Si deseas impresionarme, deberás derrotar a varias musarañas y además ayudar con las tareas de jardinería.'","Logethuil está en el Jardín de Duillond.\
\
Debes llevarle noticias de tu éxito a Logethuil.","No abandones el centro del jardín","Habla con Logethuil","Musarañas expulsadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has salido del jardín","Las botas necesarias para pisotear musarañas pueden encontrarse cerca de las escaleras del Jardín del Festival.\
\
Debes recoger las botas de la caja y arrastrarlas a tu barra de habilidades, pues las necesitarás para ahuyentar musarañas.","Has entrado en el jardín. Asegúrate de tener las botas para musarañas asignadas a tu barra de habilidades","Las musarañas molestas se encuentran en el centro del Jardín del Festival de Duillond.\
\
Logethuil te ha pedido que derrotes muchas musarañas y plantes plantitas para que el jardín prospere.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Para asignar las botas como habilidad, arrastra el objeto 'Botas de Poder Imaginable' desde tu inventario a tu barra de habilidades.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Las musarañas molestas son inmunes a cualquier otro ataque o maniobra ofensiva.</rgb>","¡Las musarañas... están por todas partes! Hay que detenerlas","Esta ronda ha terminado; no derrotaste a las musarañas a tiempo","Has plantado plantitas en montículos de tierra (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Planta plantitas en montículos de tierra (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Pisotea musarañas - el desafío","'Deberás colocarte en el centro del jardín de abajo si deseas atrapar a las musarañas molestas.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Para asignar las botas como habilidad, arrastra el objeto 'Botas de Poder Imaginable' desde tu inventario a tu barra de habilidades.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Las musarañas molestas son inmunes a cualquier otro ataque o maniobra ofensiva.</rgb>","Has recibido botas para pisotear musarañas; debes asignarlas como habilidad y entrar al jardín","Has recogido botas para pisotear musarañas","Las musarañas molestas se encuentran en el centro del Jardín del Festival de Duillond.\
\
Logethuil te ha pedido que derrotes muchas musarañas y también que protejas las tiernas plantas jóvenes que intentan crecer en este entorno hostil.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Para asignar las botas como habilidad, arrastra el objeto 'Botas de Poder Imaginable' desde tu inventario a tu barra de habilidades.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Las musarañas molestas son inmunes a cualquier otro ataque o maniobra ofensiva.</rgb>","'¿Sabes qué te aconsejo? Te aconsejo que ignores a mis amigos y te enfrentes al mayor desafío de todos. Es la única manera de ganarte mi respeto como jardinero de élite.\
\
'Cuando comiences el juego, serás responsable de las tareas de plantación y jardinería, además de expulsar a las musarañas. Si puedes lograr todo esto en el tiempo asignado, habrás hecho realmente todo lo posible por nuestro pobre jardín.\
\
'¡Da lo mejor de ti, ${PLAYER}! La apuesta es muy alta.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Las botas para pisotear musarañas aparecerán en tu inventario. Debes asignarlas a tu barra de habilidades, pues es el único ataque que funciona contra las musarañas molestas de Duillond.</rgb","Los Elfos de Duillond tienen un jardín que debería lucir hermoso para el Festival de Primavera. Lamentablemente, hace poco ha sido invadido por musarañas.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro cuando finalice el festival actual. </rgb>","Expulsa musarañas molestas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[13105]={"The Stone of Friendship","'Welcome to the Cuthstan, friend. I am Lanbert, the Sergeant of this camp.\
\
'My men have been guarding the statue from further harm, after we discovered that a band of Mountain-orcs appears to be responsible for the damage. You are welcome to stay and help us, so long as you do not put anyone in needless danger.'","'Was there some trouble in finding Lanbert? \
\
'Travel west out of Stangard and follow the road south as it forks. Stay to the path as it steers up the ridge for quite some distance, where it eventually leads into the camp.'","Lanbert is in charge of the Rohirrim camp at the Cuthstan in Wailing Hills.\
\
Gadda has asked you to seek out Lanbert at the Cuthstan.","Talk to Lanbert at the base of the Cuthstan in the Wailing Hills","Gadda is looking for someone to help a camp of men sent to protect the Cuthstan, the Stone of Friendship, in Wailing Hills, from vandals.","'There is another matter, outside of Stangard, which could use your attention, ${PLAYER}. \
\
'Are you familiar with the Stone of Friendship, the Cuthstan? It is a large stone monument in the Wailing Hills to the west, dedicated to the alliance of the Men of Gondor and the Eorlingas and to the victory at the Battle of the Field of Celebrant. This memorial has fallen under some ruin, with unseen culprits removing a section of the statue. \
\
'Men have been dispatched and have set up camp to keep watch for vandals, in the event they should return. Go there now and speak with Lanbert, Sergeant of the outpost. See what can be done to aid him in his task.'"},
[13107]={"'Hay un hombre con el que deberías hablar. Se llama Aric, pero también lo llamamos el Intérprete de piedras. Es un hombre sabio de los Eglain. En este momento está vigilando un lugar habitado por las sombras malditas de los hombres. Puede que encuentres mucho que aprender de Aric y los hombres muertos de Harloeg.\
\
'Encuentra a Aric viajando al sur a través del Gran Camino del Este y más allá de Talath Gaun. Adéntrate en Harloeg, tan al sur en el pantano como puedas viajar, y descubrirás al Intérprete de piedras en las antiguas ruinas allí.\
\
'Las sombras allí no son como las viejas historias que podrías oír sobre fantasmas... parecen no tener malas intenciones.'","Encuentra a Aric viajando al sur a través del Gran Camino del Este y más allá de Talath Gaun. Adéntrate en Harloeg, tan al sur en el pantano como puedas viajar hasta las ruinas allí.\
\
Frideric te ha enviado a hablar con Aric, el Intérprete de piedras.","El Intérprete de piedras","'Si Frideric te envía, te doy la bienvenida.\
\
'Encontrarás este lugar extraño. Las sombras de los muertos que sufrieron mucho caminan por estas ruinas, pero no temas... no te harán daño. De hecho, pueden enseñarte mucho sobre esta tierra.'","'Deberías ir a hablar con Aric, en Harloeg.'","Frideric te ha enviado a Aric, el Intérprete de piedras de los Eglain, en Harloeg."},
[13109]={"Deliver the crude stones to Stout-axe rune-carvers in Erebor (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Ambassador Spakorth wishes to offer the finely-honed skills of Stout-axe rune-carvers to Erebor.","Crude stones can be found along the western slopes of Erebor.\
\
Ambassador Spakorth has asked you to gather crude stones from the slopes of Erebor that they might be carved into rune-stones by the Stout-axes.","As Ambassador Spakorth asked, you delivered many stones of Erebor to the Stout-axe rune-carvers. Through their skill, they will be able to create impressive rune-stones for King Thorin III and Durin's Folk.","Stout-axe rune-carvers can be found in Erebor.\
\
You have gathered many stones from the slopes of Erebor and should now deliver them to the Stout-axe rune-carvers in Erebor.","You have delivered many crude stones to the Stout-axe rune-carvers.","Collected crude stones from the slopes of Erebor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Completado","Collect crude stones from the slopes of Erebor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Delivered the crude stones to Stout-axe rune-carvers in Erebor (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","The Stones of Erebor","'It has been a joy to be among the Dwarves of Durin's Folk. Each day here brings new wonders!\
\
'They seem to have taken a liking to our fondness for rune-stones, and I would not deny them more examples of our crafting skill. If you were to gather loose stones from the slopes of Erebor, our rune-carvers could shape more of them into rune-stones.\
\
'Gather as many as you can bear, and bring them to our rune-carvers. They will know what to do!'"},
[13110]={"Completed: Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel (Tier 1)","Antiguamente sede del Rey Brujo de Angmar, la temible ciudadela de Gwathrenost proyecta una larga sombra sobre la ciudad de Carn Dûm. Casi abandonada tras la deposición del Senescal de Angmar, los restos de la Corona de Hierro han salido de las sombras, buscando dominar un artefacto perdido del Rey Brujo y reclamar el dominio de Angmar.","Destroy the Shard of Tauressar","Severed from the Vandassar of Rhudaur, the shard of Tauressar is possessed of a terrible enchantment capable of swaying the hearts and minds of those who swear oaths upon it—willingly or not.\
\
You must destroy the shard of Tauressar.","With the destruction of the shard of Tauressar and the final downfall of the Iron Crown, a new day dawns in Angmar.\
\
You have completed 'Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel' on Tier 1.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You may keep this quest in your Quest Log to access each of the encounters in Gwathrenost, or you may abandon it to reset your progress. This quest will automatically reset on Monday, Thursday, and Saturday.</rgb>","Tham Mornarcham can be found atop Gwathrenost.\
\
You must ascend Gwathrenost and reach Tham Mornarcham to confront the leaders of the Iron Crown.","The Castellan's chambers can be found atop a set of winding stairs within Gwathrenost.\
\
You must find the Castellan's chambers and defeat Castellan Obáshurz if you are to confront the leaders of the Iron Crown.","Ascend Gwathrenost and enter the Castellan's chambers","The Storming of Gwathrenost (Tier 1)","Defeat Castellan Obáshurz","Ascend Gwathrenost and enter Tham Mornarcham","'There it is, ${PLAYER}. Whether it is called Tûr Dúvar, Gwathrenost, or countless other names, it is the dark citadel of the Witch-king of Angmar. But you know it well, don't you?\
\
'From what we have learned, High Priestess Ásachal has stolen a shard of the ancient Oath-stone of Rhudaur, Tauressar, and brought it to Angmar that she might wield its power as her own. It is said that it was corrupted by the hand of the Witch-king himself, and that oaths sworn upon it bind the wills of its victims to the Oath-stone. Even so far from the battle in the south-lands, our tribes learned of the Witch-king's doom. Does Ásachal truly mean to master the Oath-stone in his absence? It must be destroyed before it is too late!\
\
'Although we cannot be certain, it is likely the shard is now kept in the highest chambers of Gwathrenost. We have cleared the way, my friend. It is up to you now!'\
\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest tracks your progress for the Tier 1 difficulty of 'Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel'. While underway, it allows you to resume adventuring in 'Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel' at the furthest checkpoint you have reached in each reset cycle. Upon entering 'Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel', the first player with this quest underway to cross the bridge to Gwathrenost will determine the configuration of checkpoints and progression. This quest will automatically reset every Monday, Thursday, and Saturday.</rgb>","High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd await in Tham Mornarcham, the Seat of the the Witch-king.\
\
High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd must be defeated before they can wield the shard of Tauressar to subjugate the Free Peoples of Middle-earth.","Gurkrak keeps watch on Gwathrenost and brutally dispatches those foolish or daring enough to enter the Witch-king's citadel unbidden.\
\
You must defeat Gurkrak and enter Gwathrenost.","Defeat High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd","Defeat Gurkrak and enter Gwathrenost","One of the last remnants of the reign of the Steward of Angmar, Castellan Obáshurz tends Gwathrenost and dutifully serves his masters: High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd.\
\
You must defeat Castellan Obáshurz."},
